               & LF
               & "`undo` cleans up what is still yours. Once you hand a re"
               & "source on, its cleanup is somebody else's, but your entr"
               & "y is still registered, and there is deliberately no way "
               & "to call one off. So acquire everything fallible first, c"
               & "ommit afterwards, and let nothing fallible stand between"
               & " the commit and the end of the block."
               & LF
               & LF
               & "The usual alternative is a flag and a conditional `defer"
