               & Character'Val (226)
               & Character'Val (128)
               & Character'Val (148)
               & " `divq` divides a 128-bit dividend by a 64-bit divisor f"
               & "or a 64-bit quotient and faults when that quotient does "
               & "not fit. Either an emitted software sequence or a depend"
               & "ency on a support library, and the second contradicts D1"
               & "66, D169 and D175's standing refusal to borrow arithmeti"
               & "c this compiler does not own."
               & LF
               & "- f16 is the whole D162--D176 float programme re-run at "
               & "binary16: decimal and hexadecimal literal conversion at "
               & "p=11 and emax=15 with subnormals, D167's canonical quiet"
               & " NaN at that width, D169's rounding across a three-by-th"
