               & "ounded log builds each entry whole rather than from `zer"
               & "oed`; the entry's size is unchanged on every target, the"
               & " four-byte atom carrier taking padding the byte left. Th"
               & "e map's private bucket state is the atom set `slot_free "
               & "| slot_used | slot_dead` for the same reason, with no ch"
               & "ange to its public surface.",
            when 273 =>
               "Chosen: `core/cmp` holds `equatable`, `hashable is equat"
               & "able` and `ordered`, together with D270's shipped eviden"
               & "ce for the integer scalars, `bool` and `[]u8`. `core/map"
               & "`, `core/sort` and `core/text` import it; the map and th"
               & "e sort constrain on `cmp.hashable` and `cmp.ordered`, an"
               & "d `core/text` declares `utf8`'s three conformances again"
               & "st it. The concepts keep their declaration order, so ret"
               & "ained evidence positions do not move, and the register i"
               & "s unchanged: a program that names one of these concepts "
               & "imports `core/cmp` and with it every shipped conformance"
               & ", so a re-declaration is still D270's collision. It is a"
               & " shared module with its own consumer on every target.",
            when 274 =>
               "Chosen: a module is named by a short noun or a conventio"
               & "nal abbreviation. `core/small` is `core/spill`, whose ty"
               & "pe is `spill.list`, and `core/failing` is `core/fault`, "
               & "whose type is `fault.injector`. `core/mem.failing`, a bu"
               & "mp arena with a budget that counted only successes, is w"
               & "ithdrawn: `fault.new` over `mem.arena_over`, `fault.over"
               & "` since D288, is the one injector, and its budget spends"
               & " a permit on every call that reaches the provider, inclu"
               & "ding one the arena refuses."
               & LF
               & LF
               & "A name says what the declaration does. `mem.reserve`, a "
               & "view over caller bytes, is `mem.storage_over`, so that `"
               & "reserve` always allocates; `mem.initialized` is `mem.len"
               & "gth`; `raw_full` and `raw_not_empty` are `mem.full` and "
               & "`mem.not_empty`; `transfer_zero_prefix` is `transfer_pre"
               & "fix` for any item size, and `drain_zero_prefix` is `mem."
               & "clear`. The equality entry is `equal`, beside `less`, an"
               & "d `text.eq` is `text.equal`. `text.ordinal`, a byte offs"
               & "et that would index `utf8` as a scalar count, is `text.o"
               & "ffset`; `text.at`, which lends nothing, is `text.cursor`"
               & "; `text.written` is `text.prefix` and reports `past_end`"
               & ". `diag.note_at`, a copy, is `diag.get`; `diag.to` is `d"
               & "iag.stream`; `diag.stored` is `diag.length`. The pool's "
               & "counters are `allocations`, `frees` and `rejected_frees`"
               & ", so `frees` no longer reads as the number of free slots"
               & "."
               & LF
               & LF
               & "The map's `capacity` is D269's room: the entries that fi"
               & "t before the next new key rebuilds the table, three quar"
               & "ters of its `slots`. A new key taking a free bucket meet"
               & "s the pressure check with tombstones counted. The table "
               & "is rebuilt at its size while its live entries with the n"
               & "ew key fit in half its capacity, and grows otherwise, so"
               & " tombstones make up at least half of any pressure that r"
               & "ebuilds in place and two rebuilds are at least half a ca"
               & "pacity of operations apart. Hashes are spread with Murmu"
               & "rHash3's finalizer before reduction, since the shipped i"
               & "nteger hashes are the identity. `reserve(n)` allocates t"
               & "he smallest table whose capacity holds `n`, and counts t"
               & "he tombstones as D379 says. Release clears a storage's p"
               & "refix in constant time rather than withdrawing each item"
               & "."
               & LF
               & LF
               & "`spill.list` drops the `zeroable` constraint D152 had le"
               & "ft with no effect, so it stores pointers and atom-bearin"
               & "g records. Public signatures spell the public alias of a"
               & " private type. `mem.aligned_offset`, the bump arithmetic"
               & ", and `text.valid`, the UTF-8 check `from_bytes` makes, "
               & "are public; the hosted heap's state is opaque. A generic"
               & " routine's signature that applies one of its own paramet"
               & "ers as a type, as `storage: storage(item)` does, is L030"
               & "4 at the declaration, called or not, as the same applica"
               & "tion in a plain signature is, and a name in it that name"
               & "s nothing is that signature's L0304 or L0201 rather than"
               & " a failed match that let the program reach the lowering.",
            when 379 =>
               "Chosen: the promise is kept. After `reserve(n)`, inserti"
               & "ng new keys until `length` reaches `n` neither grows nor"
               & " rebuilds the table, as long as nothing is removed in be"
               & "tween. A table too small for `n` is replaced by the smal"
               & "lest whose capacity holds `n`, as before. A table alread"
               & "y that large keeps its size, and is rebuilt at it when i"
               & "ts tombstones and `n` together exceed its capacity, whic"
               & "h drops the tombstones; otherwise it is left alone and n"
               & "othing is allocated. Since a new key rebuilds once the l"
               & "ive entries and the tombstones reach the capacity, `n` e"
               & "ntries fit beside the tombstones exactly when the two to"
               & "gether do. A rebuild in `reserve` is an allocation like "
               & "any other: a refused one keeps every entry and tombstone"
               & ". This amends D274.",
            when 275 =>
               "Chosen: the library ships with the compiler and the comp"
               & "iler finds it. An installation is a prefix holding `bin/"
               & "refine` and `lib/landin` with the three namespaces in it"
               & "; the flake's packages and the release archive are laid "
               & "out so. `refine` asks the host for its own executable's "
               & "directory, with links resolved, and takes the first of `"
               & "../lib/landin` and, for a compiler built in a checkout, "
               & "the checkout six directories up that holds `core`. `--li"
               & "brary=DIR` names another: a build that stages only the l"
               & "ibrary modules it reaches, as the firmware lanes do, nam"
               & "es its staged tree, so the sources it hashes and debugs "
               & "are the ones compiled. A directory holding none of the t"
               & "hree is refused as a bad root is. The library root follo"
               & "ws every `--root`; an import of `core`, `hosted` or `pla"
               & "tform` resolves from it alone, and one of anything else "
               & "from the roots in their order. With no `--root`, the nam"
               & "ed files are still one module and reach the library and "
               & "whatever it imports. A `--root` naming the library's own"
               & " directory is searched once, under the user's spelling, "
               & "so a build that names the checkout records the paths it "
               & "always did. `refine version` and its JSON name the libra"
               & "ry, and the language server finds it the same way. A use"
               & "r's home root and every other default stay with the Comp"
               & "anion tool and ecosystem. Since D366 a named root holdin"
               & "g a module the library supplies is warned about, with `-"
               & "-library` as the way to compile against it.",
            when 366 =>
               "Chosen: when an import of the library is read from it an"
               & "d a named root that is not the library holds a directory"
               & " of the same module path, L0016 warns once per module at"
               & " the import that first reached it, naming the library's "
               & "directory, the root's directory that was not read, and `"
               & "--library=ROOT` as the way to compile against it. The pr"
               & "ogram is compiled as D275 says; a root that is the libra"
               & "ry itself is searched once and is not warned about.",
            when 276 =>
               "Chosen: the compiler names no host routine but one. The "
               & "public module `platform/libc` declares the C library ben"
               & "eath the hosted providers as ordinary `extern(c)` import"
               & "s: `open`, variadic as C declares it, `read` and `write`"
               & " returning `isize`, `close`, `strlen`, `malloc` returnin"
               & "g an `allocation` union whose empty arm is the atom `no_"
               & "allocation`, `free`, `stat`, and `errno_cell`, linked to"
               & " `__errno_location` on Linux and to `__error` on Darwin "
               & "and FreeBSD by `fixed if compiler.os`, which `hosted/sys"
               & "tem` reads on Darwin and FreeBSD. The errno constants `e"
               & "perm`, `enoent`, `eintr`, `eacces`, `erofs` and `enotdir"
               & "` (D287), the flags `o_rdonly` and `o_wronly`, the per-s"
               & "ystem `o_creat` and `o_trunc`, `timespec`, the per-syste"
               & "m `file_status` record and `file_status_size` are source"
               & " declarations selected by `compiler.os` and the C ABI an"
               & "d checked against each system's C headers. Like every ho"
               & "sted module it is refused on firmware (D267). `hosted/sy"
               & "stem` and `hosted/heap` reach the host only through it; "
               & "the 0666 creation mode stays in `hosted/system` as provi"
               & "der policy. On Linux `hosted/system` and `hosted/heap` u"
               & "se `platform/linux` instead (D279, D282), and since D297"
               & " both reach the host only through `platform/posix`; ever"
               & "y `platform/libc` declaration is bodyless, so a program "
               & "naming none of them needs no C library."
               & LF
               & LF
               & "`hosted/system` holds the argument root in two module ce"
               & "lls, and since D288 the process's last-error cell in a t"
               & "hird, and defines in source the public C routine `_landi"
               & "n_host_initialize_arguments`, whose signature is `(count"
               & ": i32, escaping values: ptr ptr u8) -> none`, to which D"
               & "311 adds the environment's table as a third parameter. D"
               & "208's rules are unchanged: the first nonnegative-count, "
               & "non-null-table call establishes the root without copying"
               & "; an identical repeat is a no-op; an invalid call, use b"
               & "efore initialization or replacement traps; the published"
               & " count is `max(argc - 1, 0)` without `argv[0]`. Indexed "
               & "lookup reads the `argv` entry by address and traps on a "
               & "null entry. Each of these traps is the library's own `co"
               & "mpiler.unreachable()` (D278), so a panic handler receive"
               & "s `unreachable` at a site in `hosted/system` where the b"
               & "ridge reported it at a synthetic site zero."
               & LF
               & LF
               & "The compiler's one hosted contract is that call. When a "
               & "hosted entry is selected and the program defines a C rou"
               & "tine with the link symbol `_landin_host_initialize_argum"
               & "ents`, the hosted `main` calls it with its incoming `arg"
               & "c` and `argv`, and since D311 its `envp`, before its bod"
               & "y. A program that defines none calls nothing, so a hoste"
               & "d program that never imports `hosted/system` links witho"
               & "ut it. Beside a hosted entry every declaration carrying "
               & "that symbol must be exactly `extern(c) (i32, ptr ptr u8)"
               & " -> none`, with `escaping` immaterial, or it is refused "
               & "with L0347. The symbol is an ordinary default-visibility"
               & " global rather than a hidden one, and a C-owned `main` s"
               & "till calls it explicitly. The names `strlen`, `malloc`, "
               & "`free`, `open`, `read`, `write`, `close` and the errno a"
               & "ccessor are no longer set aside for the backend: they ar"
               & "e `platform/libc`'s imports, and ordinary symbol allocat"
               & "ion keeps a private Landin definition of the same spelli"
               & "ng from capturing them.",
            when 277 =>
               "Chosen: `hosted/heap` performs the same over-allocation "
               & "in source over `platform/libc`'s `malloc` and `free` (D2"
               & "76). It asks `malloc` for the request plus `alignment - "
               & "1` bytes and one `usize` word, refusing with `mem.out_of"
               & "_memory` before the call an addition that would overflow"
               & " or a total above `(0 -% 1) >> 1`, the host's `PTRDIFF_M"
               & "AX`. It aligns within the block and writes the address `"
               & "malloc` returned into the word before the aligned block "
               & "a byte at a time, because for an alignment that is not a"
               & " multiple of the word the word is unaligned; release rea"
               & "ds it back the same way and passes it to `free`. A `no_a"
               & "llocation` result is `mem.out_of_memory`. D195's contrac"
               & "t is unchanged: every `usize` alignment is accepted, zer"
               & "o and one meaning byte alignment, and a zero-byte reques"
               & "t returns a distinct non-null token. On Linux, D282 repl"
               & "aces this provider, and D300 replaces it on Darwin and F"
               & "reeBSD too.",
            when 278 =>
               "Chosen: `compiler.unreachable()` on the toolchain module"
               & " [1560], with no import and no keyword. It types as a ca"
               & "ll of a `() -> noreturn` routine: a statement, the value"
               & " of an `if` or `match` arm, or the end of any path, and "
               & "definite assignment, named results and `noreturn` bodies"
               & " treat it as not returning. It takes no arguments; misus"
               & "e is refused as the same misuse of such a routine would "
               & "be, L0327 for an argument, L0331 for a value and L0329 f"
               & "or `try` or `else`, and naming it without calling it is "
               & "L0203. Reaching it raises `unreachable` through D232 at "
               & "its own numbered site, with the panic map entry a compil"
               & "er check has, or the terminal default trap when no handl"
               & "er is selected. It is a statement and not a check, so `u"
               & "nchecked` never removes it. It is available on every tar"
               & "get, firmware included. `hosted/system` stops on every m"
               & "isuse of the argument root with it.",
            when 279 =>
               "Chosen: the public module `platform/linux` declares Linu"
               & "x's system calls in source, inside `fixed if compiler.os"
               & " == linux`. It declares nothing on Darwin and FreeBSD, a"
               & "nd because Landin has no conditional import, `hosted/sys"
               & "tem` and `hosted/heap` import it on every hosted system."
               & " Each call is one ordinary assembly block: x86-64 `sysca"
               & "ll` with the number in rax, arguments in rdi, rsi, rdx, "
               & "r10, r8 and r9, and rcx and r11 overwritten; arm64 `svc "
               & "#0` with the number in x8 and arguments in x0"
               & Character'Val (226)
               & Character'Val (128)
               & Character'Val (147)
               & "x5; RV64 `ecall` with the number in x17 (a7) and argumen"
               & "ts in x10"
               & Character'Val (226)
               & Character'Val (128)
               & Character'Val (147)
               & "x15 (a0"
               & Character'Val (226)
               & Character'Val (128)
               & Character'Val (147)
               & "a5). rax, x0 or a0 carries the result. Its wrappers are "
               & "`read`, `write`, `openat`, `close`, `statx`, `mmap`, `mu"
               & "nmap` and the `noreturn` `exit_group`, to which D294 add"
               & "s `getdents64`, `mkdirat` and `unlinkat`, a public raw `"
               & "system_call` and every call's number. A failure is minus"
               & " its errno in the result; there is no errno cell. The `*"
               & "at` calls take `at_fdcwd`, and `statx`'s `file_status` i"
               & "s the kernel's one 256-byte record on every architecture"
               & ". Every public routine has the link name `_landin_linux_"
               & "` followed by its own name, so none of them replaces the"
               & " C library's function of the same spelling when a progra"
               & "m also links libc."
               & LF
               & LF
               & "The module owns the process entry. `_landin_start` is a "
               & "naked routine that clears the frame pointer (and the lin"
               & "k register on arm64 and RV64), aligns the stack where th"
               & "e ABI requires it and calls `_landin_start_main` with th"
               & "e initial stack's address. That routine reads argc, argv"
               & ", envp and the auxiliary vector after envp's terminator,"
               & " keeps the environment and auxiliary roots for `environm"
               & "ent()` and `auxiliary(tag)`, and calls C's view of the p"
               & "rogram's entry: a bodyless `extern(c) link(symbol: ""main"
               & """)` of `(i32, ptr ptr u8, ptr ptr u8) -> i32`, which the"
               & " checker admits beside the native hosted `main` as the s"
               & "ame symbol. It ends the process with `exit_group` and ma"
               & "in's result. No C library initialisation runs and no thr"
               & "ead-local storage exists. Under `--link=libc` (D280) the"
               & " C runtime starts the program, and the argument initiali"
               & "zer passes `platform/linux.adopt_start` the `argc`, `arg"
               & "v` and `envp` C's `main` was given (D311). It takes the "
               & "environment and the auxiliary vector after `envp`'s null"
               & " only when the tables have the initial stack's layout: `"
               & "argv` above the calling frame, `envp` directly after `ar"
               & "gv`'s null, at least one string and every string above t"
               & "he tables, AT_NULL within 64 entries below the lowest st"
               & "ring with every tag below 4096, AT_PAGESZ a power of two"
               & " of at least 4096, and AT_RANDOM's sixteen bytes between"
               & " the vector and the lowest string. Nothing above the low"
               & "est string is read. Otherwise `environment()` is `no_env"
               & "ironment`, `auxiliary` finds nothing and `page_size()` f"
               & "alls back to 4096. The alternatives were the C library's"
               & " `getauxval`, which a static link would refuse with L050"
               & "0 since nothing tells the library its link mode; `PR_GET"
               & "_AUXV`, Linux 6.4's; `/proc/self/auxv`, which needs `/pr"
               & "oc`; and trusting any `envp`, which `setenv` may have mo"
               & "ved and a C `main` may have built, sending reads into un"
               & "mapped memory. `abi/auxiliary-from-c` pins the adoption "
               & "and each refusal."
               & LF
               & LF
               & "Naked routines are admitted on hosted x86-64, arm64 and "
               & "RV64 for this entry. Their text is the routine's whole b"
               & "ody followed by a trap, keeps [1990]'s uniform text rule"
               & "s except that it may transfer control, and takes no oper"
               & "ands. Their CFI marks the return address undefined, so a"
               & " debugger's stack ends at `_landin_start`.",
            when 280 =>
               "Chosen: `--link=static|libc` chooses how a hosted execut"
               & "able is linked. Linux defaults to `static`: the driver l"
               & "oads `platform/linux` from the compiler's library (D275)"
               & " and links with `-nostdlib -static -no-pie -Wl,-e,_landi"
               & "n_start` and `-Wl,--gc-sections`, with no C runtime obje"
               & "ct, no C library and no dynamic loader. `--link=libc` ke"
               & "eps the C runtime's link. Darwin and FreeBSD reach their"
               & " systems only through their C libraries and link with `l"
               & "ibc`, their only mode; `--link=static` there is a usage "
               & "error, as is `--link` on a target with no hosted system "
               & "or without `--emit=exe` or `--emit=asm`. A static reques"
               & "t is refused with L0500 before any tool runs, naming `--"
               & "link=libc`, when no library holding `platform/linux` was"
               & " found, when the program asks for `linker.library`, or w"
               & "hen it refers to a bodyless external symbol no program i"
               & "tem defines. The refusal counts only what the entry reac"
               & "hes, since every backend collects per-item sections (D30"
               & "3), and names each missing symbol with the routine that "
               & "refers to it, `dlopen, which platform/posix's open_libra"
               & "ry refers to`, so a program loading a library learns whi"
               & "ch of its calls asked for the C library (D336). `-v`, `-"
               & "-dry-run` and the build report name the mode. An emitted"
               & " `.s` under static mode includes `platform/linux` and st"
               & "ill links under a C driver. `refine check` gives the ref"
               & "usals of a C library asked for and of a C symbol nothing"
               & " defines, as compiling does (D443).",
            when 362 =>
               "Chosen: on a hosted target the assembly is removed once "
               & "the link has run, whether it succeeded or not, unless `-"
               & "-keep-asm` asks to keep it, or a source map is written b"
               & "eside the executable (`--debug`, `--panic-map` or caller"
               & " coordinates), since the map names that assembly by its "
               & "hash and is resolved against it. Firmware keeps it with "
               & "the object, linker script and map its link writes beside"
               & " the image, which its build report reads. `--keep-asm` b"
               & "elongs to an executable; with `--emit=asm` or `--emit=ir"
               & "` it is a misuse. A dry run says `remove` after the link"
               & " it plans."
               & LF
               & LF
               & "`refine compile PROGRAM.s -o PROGRAM` links one assembly"
               & " file as a compiled program's assembly is linked: the sa"
               & "me driver choice, the same arguments for the request's `"
               & "--target`, `--level`, `--link`, `--linker` and `--debug`"
               & ", and the same protection of an existing executable and "
               & "of the operand itself. A file is assembly when its name "
               & "ends in `.s`; it must be the one operand, without `--roo"
               & "t`, and options that describe compiling Landin source (`"
               & "--optimize`, `--specialize`, `--build-mode`, `--option`,"
               & " `--build-report`, `--stage-report`, `--stack-report`, `"
               & "--panic-map`, `--depfile`, `--firmware-entry` and `--kee"
               & "p-asm`) are refused with it. The operand is never read b"
               & "y the compiler and never removed. A program's `linker.li"
               & "brary` archives are not recorded in its assembly, so an "
               & "assembly file is linked without them.",
            when 364 =>
               "Chosen: with no `--toolchain`, a Linux target tries, in "
               & "order, the target's own triplet driver, `MACHINE-linux-g"
               & "nu-gcc`, `MACHINE-redhat-linux-gcc` and the `pc` or `unk"
               & "nown` vendor's spelling, each a GCC that drives the asse"
               & "mbler and linker for that machine alone, and then `gcc` "
               & "only when the target is the compiler's own host (D257), "
               & "where the host's GCC is a driver for it; a cross target "
               & "never falls back to the host's compiler, which would ass"
               & "emble for the wrong machine. It is `gcc` and not `cc` be"
               & "cause the link passes the GNU assembler's options. The f"
               & "irst one the host can start is the one run; a dry run na"
               & "mes it, or the first looked for when none can be. `--too"
               & "lchain=NAME` is still the only one tried. Darwin keeps A"
               & "pple's `/usr/bin/clang`, FreeBSD its triplet's Clang and"
               & " Cortex-M `arm-none-eabi-gcc`."
               & LF
               & LF
               & "Whether a driver can be started is asked once the progra"
               & "m is known to need it, after every refusal of the progra"
               & "m itself, D280's static refusals of a C symbol, `linker."
               & "library` and a missing `platform/linux` among them, and "
               & "before anything is written. A target that names no drive"
               & "r is still refused before any source is read. With none "
               & "found, L0500 names every driver looked for and what to i"
               & "nstall: the distribution's GCC on the compiler's own hos"
               & "t (`apt install gcc`, `dnf install gcc`), its cross comp"
               & "iler for another Linux machine (`apt install gcc-aarch64"
               & "-linux-gnu`), Apple's command line tools on Darwin, and "
               & "the Arm embedded GCC for Cortex-M.",
            when 281 =>
               "Chosen: an ordinary RV64 assembly block admits `ecall`. "
               & "Like x86-64's `syscall` and arm64's `svc`, it enters the"
               & " kernel and returns to the next instruction, so the bloc"
               & "k stays straight-line. `ebreak`, `c.ebreak`, `mret` and "
               & "the other control transfers stay refused.",
            when 282 =>
               "Chosen: on Linux `hosted/heap` maps its own memory, now "
               & "through `platform/posix`, which makes `platform/linux`'s"
               & " calls (D279, D297). It keeps eight size classes from 32"
               & " to 4096 bytes. A class with no free slot maps a 64 KiB "
               & "chunk and links its slots into a free list; a freed slot"
               & " returns to its class's list and is handed out before an"
               & "y new chunk is mapped; chunks are never unmapped. A requ"
               & "est whose extent exceeds 4096 bytes is a mapping of its "
               & "own, rounded to the page size and unmapped when freed. T"
               & "wo words precede every block, the slot's or mapping's st"
               & "art and its extent, at the multiple of the word at or be"
               & "low a header before the block, so they are aligned whate"
               & "ver the block's alignment and every `usize` alignment wo"
               & "rks, a power of two or not; a zero-byte request is a dis"
               & "tinct token. An addition that would overflow, or an exte"
               & "nt above `PTRDIFF_MAX` less the page rounding, is `mem.o"
               & "ut_of_memory` before any state changes, as is a failed m"
               & "apping. The provider was single-threaded; D502 puts its "
               & "classes behind a lock once a thread has started. D300 ma"
               & "kes it the heap of every hosted system.",
            when 283 =>
               "Chosen: zero-image module data are laid out smallest fir"
               & "st, ties in item order, on x86-64 and RV64, so one objec"
               & "t as large as RIP-relative or `auipc` addressing reaches"
               & " cannot push another datum out of reach. arm64's "
               & Character'Val (194)
               & Character'Val (177)
               & "4 GiB reach is unchanged. The implicit `platform/linux` "
               & "roots of a static link (D280) exposed it.",
            when 296 =>
               "Chosen: when the entry module declares a public `main`, "
               & "a module routine, generic instance, evidence table or bi"
               & "nding is lowered and emitted only if the program can rea"
               & "ch it. The roots are every routine the entry module defi"
               & "nes, so `main`, D232's `panic_handler` and a firmware en"
               & "try among them; a binding with a link symbol; a C defini"
               & "tion that is public or has a link symbol; a definition i"
               & "n a machine convention, as the process entry `_landin_st"
               & "art` is; a definition whose link name a bodyless import "
               & "names; a routine or binding with a placement, a section,"
               & " an alignment, a vector or `keep`; one whose name or lin"
               & "k name, or `_` and either on Mach-O, is a word in an `as"
               & "sembler.block`'s text; and every module declaration that"
               & " is neither a routine nor a binding, a type whose length"
               & " names a constant among them. A reached routine or bindi"
               & "ng reaches what any resolved reference in it names, in a"
               & "ny position, the generic instance any of its calls selec"
               & "ts, and the conformance whose table a selection, an `any"
               & "` construction or a `for` reads; a reached instance reac"
               & "hes its template and the conformances it receives; a rea"
               & "ched conformance reaches its providers and, for an erase"
               & "d table, D145's parent conformances. `public` alone is n"
               & "ot a use, and neither is a native routine's link symbol,"
               & " which [1975] makes its linker identity rather than an e"
               & "xport. Every declaration is still checked, so an unreach"
               & "ed declaration's errors are still errors. Reachability c"
               & "an keep too much but never too little, and kept items ar"
               & "e numbered in declaration order, so the output stays a f"
               & "unction of the sources. Any compilation without a public"
               & " `main` keeps everything.",
            when 303 =>
               "Chosen: the ELF backends for x86-64, arm64 and RV64, on "
               & "Linux and FreeBSD, give every routine, datum and evidenc"
               & "e table its own section, named by item index so the outp"
               & "ut stays a function of the sources, with zero-image data"
               & " in their own `.bss` sections; Mach-O keeps `.subsection"
               & "s_via_symbols` and Darwin links with `-dead_strip`; Cort"
               & "ex-M keeps its per-item sections under its own script. E"
               & "very ELF link passes `--gc-sections`. A static link's L0"
               & "500 counts only the references the entry reaches, from `"
               & "_landin_start`, `main`, the argument initializer, `panic"
               & "_handler`, every `keep` item, every datum and the entrie"
               & "s D374 keeps of every evidence table, through calls and "
               & "taken addresses, an external C name leading to the routi"
               & "ne that defines it.",
            when 284 =>
               "Chosen: `platform/linux`'s `_landin_start_main` holds th"
               & "e processor to the executable's level before `main` runs"
               & ". The level is the compile-time `compiler.feature` facts"
               & ": `fixed if` selects, for each level, its name, its chec"
               & "ks and its `check_level`, and the baseline's `check_leve"
               & "l` is empty, so a baseline executable runs no check. On "
               & "x86-64 the check reads `cpuid` leaves 1, 7 and 0x8000000"
               & "1 for D255's v2, v3 and v4 features in D255's order, and"
               & " above v2 requires the system to save the state the leve"
               & "l uses: OSXSAVE and XCR0's SSE and AVX bits for v3, and "
               & "the opmask and ZMM bits for v4, read with `xgetbv`. On a"
               & "rm64 it reads AT_HWCAP for armv8.1-a's atomics, CRC32 an"
               & "d RDM. On RV64 it asks `riscv_hwprobe` for Zba, and a ke"
               & "rnel that cannot answer does not confirm the level; no L"
               & "inux interface reports XTheadBa, so it is not checked. A"
               & " processor without a feature writes one line to standard"
               & " error, `landin: this executable needs LEVEL, and the pr"
               & "ocessor lacks FEATURE`, and ends the process with status"
               & " 127, the status glibc's loader gives when it refuses an"
               & " executable's ISA level, so a static and a libc build of"
               & " one program end alike on one machine. Under `--link=lib"
               & "c` the C runtime starts the program, the loader's note a"
               & "pplies on x86-64, and the entry check does not run. `lev"
               & "el`, `read_cpu_words` and `missing_feature` are public, "
               & "so the check can be tested on injected words.",
            when 285 =>
               "Chosen: `process` gains `input: (self: provider) -> (str"
               & "eam: file)`, taking the handle by value as every I/O ent"
               & "ry does (D288), read through `reader` like any opened fi"
               & "le: zero from a nonempty read is the end of input. `host"
               & "ed/system` answers descriptor 0. `core/io.memory` answer"
               & "s handle 0 over the caller's `input` bytes, the argument"
               & " `memory_over` takes after the argument table; the `read"
               & "_limit` and `fail_read_at` of its `io.memory_space` appl"
               & "y to it as to a file, and closing it ends it. The five f"
               & "ree functions `io.input`, `io.out`, `io.err`, `io.argume"
               & "nt_count` and `io.argument_at` take the handle `in` as `"
               & "host: provider`, as `io.read`, `io.write` and the `files"
               & "` functions do, so a caller always passes the handle, `i"
               & "o.write(host, io.out(host), ...)`, and nothing is locked"
               & "; `argument_at` lends its result `from host`, and two ar"
               & "guments lent from one handle are live at once. A runtime"
               & " or ABI fixture names the file its program reads as stan"
               & "dard input with `stdin:`, relative to the fixture and be"
               & "low it; without the key every lane gives the program an "
               & "empty input, never the harness's own. A fixture that rea"
               & "ds standard input is hosted: firmware refuses it by name"
               & " (D267) and the memory provider runs the same routine th"
               & "ere.",
            when 286 =>
               "Chosen: `text.write_u64` and `text.write_usize` have `wr"
               & "ite_u32`'s shape: they count the digits by division and "
               & "report `no_space` before writing. `text.parse_u32`, `par"
               & "se_u64` and `parse_usize` read decimal digits from `[]u8"
               & "` and report `invalid_number` or `number_overflow`, whic"
               & "hever the scan from the left meets first; `usize` is the"
               & " target's width, so firmware parses 32 bits. `to_u32` ov"
               & "er `utf8` parses the text's bytes. `core/diag`'s positio"
               & "n writer, the derived hosted program and the fizzbuzz an"
               & "d fannkuch writers use them; the configuration parser ke"
               & "eps its recursive digit parser, which the debugger sessi"
               & "ons stop in. D355 retires the slice writers: the builder"
               & "'s appends are the one decimal writer, and the parses li"
               & "ve with the signed and hexadecimal ones.",
            when 287 =>
               "Chosen: ENOTDIR, 20 on Linux, Darwin and FreeBSD, is `no"
               & "t_found` from `open_read` and `open_write`, and an outpu"
               & "t path that meets it is absent, so `same_file` answers f"
               & "alse. `last_errno` still holds 20 for a caller that need"
               & "s the difference.",
            when 288 =>
               "Chosen: a value that is edited, a container or a bounded"
               & " log, stays `inout`. A service is a handle: a small copy"
               & "able record, passed `in`, that refers to its state throu"
               & "gh a pointer and whose lifetime is checked once, where i"
               & "t is made from that state. `mem.allocator`'s `alloc`, `g"
               & "row` and `free` and every entry of `core/io`'s `reader`,"
               & " `writer`, `files` and `process` take `self: provider` b"
               & "y value, and a conformance changes state through the han"
               & "dle. Free functions take `memory: provider` for an alloc"
               & "ator and `host: provider` for I/O, passed `in`, and `cor"
               & "e/vec`, `core/map`, `core/tree` and `core/spill` take `m"
               & "emory: provider`; a call is spelled as before."
               & LF
               & LF
               & "Caller-owned state is a type the caller declares `zeroed"
               & "`; `over` takes it `inout`, fills it and returns the han"
               & "dle `from` it. `mem.arena_space` and `mem.arena` have `a"
               & "rena_over(inout state, escaping base, size) -> (handle: "
               & "arena from state, base)` and `arena_over_unchecked` with"
               & " a plain `base`; `pool.space` and `pool.provider` have `"
               & "pool.over(inout state, base, extent, slot_size, slot_cou"
               & "nt, slot_alignment, bookkeeping)`, which reports `mem.ou"
               & "t_of_memory` before changing the state; `fault.space` an"
               & "d `fault.injector(P)` have `fault.over(inout state, inne"
               & "r, allowed_attempts)`; `region.space(fixed capacity)` an"
               & "d `region.region(P)` have `region.over(inout state, pare"
               & "nt)` and `region.release(inout state, parent)`, a capaci"
               & "ty of zero growing the ledger through the parent and a p"
               & "ositive one holding that many records in the state; and "
               & "`io.memory_space` and `io.memory` have `memory_over(inou"
               & "t state, files, arguments, input, output, errors)`. `io."
               & "memory_space` is public, so its limits, failure points a"
               & "nd counters may be read and set while the handle lives; "
               & "the handles are opaque. A state type holds only scalars,"
               & " because `zeroed` has no image for a pointer, a slice or"
               & " a pointer union (L0328), so a reference the caller supp"
               & "lies lives in the handle. Since the handle is `from` its"
               & " state, returning it past that state is L0314, and `rele"
               & "ase`, which takes the state `inout`, is L0315 while the "
               & "handle is still used; using the handle is an `in` use an"
               & "d locks nothing."
               & LF
               & LF
               & "A provider stacked on another holds a copy of the other'"
               & "s handle: the region, the injector, `io.writer_of`'s len"
               & "t writer, `writer_of(host: any world) -> (adapter: lent_"
               & "writer from host)`, and `diag.stream(host: any io.writer"
               & ", where_to: io.file) -> (result: streaming from host)`, "
               & "which takes both by value. `region.release` takes the pa"
               & "rent again because a zeroable state cannot hold the pare"
               & "nt's handle (L0328), and keeping the parent in caller st"
               & "ate through an `escaping` parameter would refuse every f"
               & "rame-local parent with L0314. The `diag.log` concept kee"
               & "ps `self: ptr mut logger`, because a bounded log is an e"
               & "dited value. Process-wide state belongs to the process, "
               & "so its handles borrow nothing and are bound without `mut"
               & "`: `system.new()` returns a handle holding the argument "
               & "table, its count and the process's last-error cell, `hea"
               & "p.new()` is unchanged, and the Linux heap's size classes"
               & " are module state (D282). An erased capability is built "
               & "from the address of a handle binding, `any(addr host)`, "
               & "which D289 dispatches; an immutable binding suffices."
               & LF
               & LF
               & "The last error is the one value the system provider writ"
               & "es on behalf of its caller, so the handle names the cell"
               & " it records into, `failure: ptr mut i32`, and `system.la"
               & "st_errno(host)` reads that cell. Every handle from `syst"
               & "em.new()` shares the process's cell, a private module `m"
               & "ut` of `hosted/system`. `system.over(inout state: system"
               & ".space) -> (handle: system from state)` fills a caller-d"
               & "eclared, zeroable `system.space` holding one `failure: i"
               & "32` and returns a handle that records its last error the"
               & "re instead, for a C thread calling into Landin or a libr"
               & "ary that keeps its own detail. Either handle shares the "
               & "process's arguments and descriptors, and either traps be"
               & "fore the argument root exists. D207's thread-local meani"
               & "ng is therefore kept by ownership until thread-local sto"
               & "rage exists: a thread over its own cell reads only its o"
               & "wn failures."
               & LF
               & LF
               & "An allocation still borrows nothing from its allocator: "
               & "[0810]'s integer conversion is kept. A block returned `f"
               & "rom self` and kept in a container's `inout` storage woul"
               & "d be L0314, and making the handle `escaping` to allow it"
               & " would refuse every handle over frame-local state.",
            when 293 =>
               "Chosen: `io.directories` is a fifth concept, outside `wo"
               & "rld`, with `open_directory`, `read_entry`, `entry_size`,"
               & " `close_directory`, `make_directory`, `remove_file` and "
               & "`remove_directory`; the listing consumer has to build an"
               & "d clear its own tree. Its provider is a handle (D288); a"
               & "n open `io.directory` is a value the caller edits. `open"
               & "_directory(host, path, buffer)` returns a directory `fro"
               & "m` a buffer the caller supplies, `read_entry` takes it `"
               & "inout` and returns an entry whose name is lent `from` it"
               & " until the next read, and `close_directory` takes it `si"
               & "nk`. An entry is its name as `[]u8` and its kind, `regul"
               & "ar | subdirectory | symbolic_link | special`, never foll"
               & "owing a link; where the file system records no kind the "
               & "provider asks the entry itself, and skips one removed in"
               & " between. An empty name is the end of the directory, as "
               & "zero bytes is the end of a read; `.` and `..` are never "
               & "entries. `entry_size` gives a `u64` relative to the open"
               & " directory without following a link, and a name that is "
               & "empty, holds `/` or NUL, or is 1,024 bytes or longer is "
               & "`not_found` without asking the host. `io.directory_buffe"
               & "r` is 1,024 bytes, the hosted providers' smallest buffer"
               & ", which every hosted system's entries fit. A missing pat"
               & "h or a file used as a directory is `not_found` (D287), E"
               & "PERM, EACCES and EROFS are `no_access`, a name `make_dir"
               & "ectory` finds taken is the new atom `io.already_exists`,"
               & " and anything else is `io_failed` with its errno kept. A"
               & " directory dropped without `close_directory` keeps its d"
               & "escriptor until the process ends; `defer io.close_direct"
               & "ory(...)` is the idiom. On Linux, `getdents64` fills the"
               & " caller's buffer, and every record is held to lie inside"
               & " what was filled, to be long enough for its header and t"
               & "o end its name inside itself, so a bad record is `io_fai"
               & "led` rather than a trap. Darwin and FreeBSD open with `O"
               & "_DIRECTORY` and read through `fdopendir`, `readdir` and "
               & "`closedir`, copying each name into the caller's buffer, "
               & "and make and remove with `mkdirat` and `unlinkat`. The m"
               & "emory provider's directories are the slot names' parts b"
               & "efore a `/`, and a slot ending in `/` is an empty direct"
               & "ory; it refuses changes other than an existing directory"
               & "'s `already_exists` with `no_access`, so `memory_over` k"
               & "eeps its signature.",
            when 294 =>
               "Chosen: the raw call is public as `system_call`, six int"
               & "eger arguments and an integer result, minus the errno on"
               & " failure. `platform/linux/numbers` names every call's nu"
               & "mber for x86-64, arm64 and RV64 by one rule, the kernel'"
               & "s table name followed by `_number`, which no reserved wo"
               & "rd or wrapper can meet. The numbers are generated by `sc"
               & "ripts/linux_syscalls.py` from a pinned kernel release's "
               & "own tables, x86-64's `syscall_64.tbl` with the common an"
               & "d 64 ABIs and the generic table for arm64 and RV64 with "
               & "each architecture's own entries, and the generated file "
               & "names the release and its checksum; the generator can ch"
               & "eck the committed file instead of writing it. With no re"
               & "lease named it holds `numbers.ldn` to being its own rend"
               & "ering under the pin and writes or checks the wrappers fr"
               & "om it, so adding a typed wrapper needs no kernel source;"
               & " the release is needed only to change the pin. The wrapp"
               & "ers take their numbers from the same tables, through a p"
               & "rivate generated file, so there is one source of numbers"
               & ". The numbers are a module of their own, imported by a p"
               & "rogram that calls by number, so `platform/linux` stays t"
               & "he wrappers every static Linux program imports; a progra"
               & "m pays only for the numbers it uses (D296). Typed wrappe"
               & "rs stay for the calls the library itself makes, `getdent"
               & "s64`, `mkdirat` and `unlinkat` among them.",
            when 297 =>
               "Chosen: four layers. Each system's own interface stays r"
               & "aw under `platform/`: `platform/linux` with its numbers "
               & "(D279, D294) and `platform/libc` (D276). `platform/posix"
               & "` gives POSIX's facilities in Landin types, written once"
               & " over each (D298). The portable concepts in `core` name "
               & "no POSIX type, so `io.file` is a `distinct usize`, an op"
               & "en directory holds a `handle: usize`, and no integer des"
               & "criptor, mode bit, owner, signal number or errno is in a"
               & " `core` signature. `hosted/system` and `hosted/heap` are"
               & " written once over `platform/posix`, with no code of the"
               & "ir own for any system. All three `platform` modules are "
               & "scoped to the hosted POSIX systems, Linux, Darwin and Fr"
               & "eeBSD, by namespace and by a `compiler.assert`, and firm"
               & "ware refuses them by name with L0015; `platform/libc` se"
               & "rves Linux too, under `--link=libc`. Every public routin"
               & "e of `platform/posix` has a `_landin_posix_` link name, "
               & "so none replaces a C library function of the same spelli"
               & "ng. A BSD and Darwin module for kqueue comes with the ev"
               & "ent-driven Io that needs it.",
            when 298 =>
               "Chosen: `posix.descriptor` is a `distinct i32`, with `st"
               & "andard_input`, `standard_output`, `standard_error` and `"
               & "working_directory`, the `*at` calls' AT_FDCWD. Every err"
               & "no any of the three systems defines is an atom named aft"
               & "er its C macro in lower case, 154 of them and `unlisted`"
               & ", in the atom set `posix.errno`; an alias has no atom of"
               & " its own, so EWOULDBLOCK is `eagain`, and ENOTSUP is its"
               & " own atom only on Darwin. `number` gives an atom's numbe"
               & "r on this system and `errno_of` a number's atom, through"
               & " tables generated from Linux's, FreeBSD's and Darwin's h"
               & "eaders. The calls are POSIX's own: `open_at`, `read`, `w"
               & "rite`, `close`, `status_at` with a `status` of device, i"
               & "node, kind and size, the directory calls over a caller's"
               & " buffer, which list `.` and `..` as POSIX does, `make_di"
               & "rectory_at`, `unlink_at`, `remove_directory_at`, `map`, "
               & "`unmap`, `page_size`, `exit` and `poll`, whose events ar"
               & "e a `distinct u16` flag set (D302). None retries EINTR o"
               & "r completes a short transfer; that is provider policy in"
               & " `hosted/system`. Each path is copied with its NUL into "
               & "a per-system `PATH_MAX` buffer, so the terminator never "
               & "reaches a caller; a path holding a NUL is `einval` and o"
               & "ne too long `enametoolong`. The argument root lives here"
               & ", with the environment's table since D311, read from the"
               & " initial stack on a static Linux program and through the"
               & " C runtime otherwise, as a real `ptr ptr u8` (D301).",
            when 299 =>
               "Chosen: `text.host_string` is one opaque type whose repr"
               & "esentation is chosen in one place by target, bytes on ev"
               & "ery system today, so a 16-bit representation for Windows"
               & " goes there. `text.host_over` makes one lending its byte"
               & "s, `text.host_bytes` gives the bytes back, `text.from_ho"
               & "st` converts to `utf8` and fails `invalid_text` when it "
               & "is not, and `text.host_equal` compares with a literal. E"
               & "very path the `files` and `directories` concepts take, e"
               & "very argument and every directory entry's name is a host"
               & " string, so a value passed from an argument to `open` is"
               & " never converted. `io.terminate_path`, the `_bytes` and "
               & "`_text` open variants, `io.copy_argument`, `io.argument`"
               & " and the atoms `empty_path`, `path_contains_nul`, `path_"
               & "too_long` and `argument_too_long` are withdrawn; those c"
               & "ases are now the system's own answer, `not_found` for EN"
               & "OENT and `io_failed` for EINVAL and ENAMETOOLONG, their "
               & "errno kept. The memory provider's argument table is `[]["
               & "]u8`, which firmware can declare as static data.",
            when 300 =>
               "Chosen: D282's size-class heap is the heap of every host"
               & "ed system, over `platform/posix`'s `map` and `unmap`, so"
               & " `hosted/heap` has no code of its own for any system. It"
               & " is single-threaded everywhere; a heap that threads shar"
               & "e is the threads item's, on every system alike, which D5"
               & "02 and D514 give it.",
            when 304 =>
               "Chosen: `mem.copy(into, source)` copies with `memmove`'s"
               & " rule, from the last byte down when the destination star"
               & "ts inside the source after its first byte and from the f"
               & "irst up when it starts at or before the source, so overl"
               & "ap is always safe; one wholly after the source may go ei"
               & "ther way. It fails `out_of_bounds` before writing when `"
               & "into` is shorter; a longer destination keeps its tail. `"
               & "mem.fill` sets every byte. `cmp.compare` answers the ato"
               & "m set `less | equal | greater`, bytes unsigned and a pro"
               & "per prefix first. `mem.find` gives the first match's ind"
               & "ex or the source's length, so `source[0..<find("
               & Character'Val (226)
               & Character'Val (128)
               & Character'Val (166)
               & ")]` is always valid.",
            when 305 =>
               "Chosen: `text.builder` is a value the caller edits `inou"
               & "t`. `text.over(buffer)` makes one bounded by the caller'"
               & "s buffer, and `text.growing(allocator)` one that starts "
               & "empty and doubles through an erased `mem.allocator`, res"
               & "izing its storage through the allocator, which grows it "
               & "in place or moves it (D337), and given back with `text.r"
               & "elease`. Bytes, a byte, `utf8`, host strings, signed and"
               & " unsigned decimals of every width and lower-case hexadec"
               & "imal are appended; each piece is written whole or not at"
               & " all, failing `no_space` with the builder unchanged, whi"
               & "ch is also a growing builder's answer when its allocator"
               & " refuses. `text.align_right` and `text.align_left` pad w"
               & "hat was written since an earlier `text.length`. The allo"
               & "cator is erased because the `formattable` entry must nam"
               & "e one builder type.",
            when 306 =>
               "Chosen: `text.format(into, template, values)` writes `te"
               & "mplate` into a builder with each `{}` replaced by the ne"
               & "xt value, an `any text.formattable` whose one entry appe"
               & "nds the value; `{{` and `}}` are a brace. The whole temp"
               & "late is checked before anything is written: a count that"
               & " disagrees with the values, or a stray brace, is `invali"
               & "d_format` and writes nothing, and `no_space` part-way re"
               & "stores the builder's earlier length. Width, fill and rad"
               & "ix are the builder's typed calls, not the template's. Th"
               & "e integer types, `bool`, `utf8`, `[]u8` and host strings"
               & " conform. Formatting is the same in every locale and kee"
               & "ps no global state.",
            when 307 =>
               "Chosen: `core/text` parses signed and unsigned decimals "
               & "of every width and hexadecimal over bytes. A signed valu"
               & "e takes an optional `-` and never a `+`, because no appe"
               & "nd writes one, and `-0` is zero; hexadecimal takes eithe"
               & "r case and no prefix. Overflow is found during the scan "
               & "against the type's own limit, so the first problem from "
               & "the left is the one reported, as `number_overflow` or `i"
               & "nvalid_number`.",
            when 308 =>
               "Chosen: `io.buffered_writer(provider)` is a value edited"
               & " `inout` over a writer's handle and a caller's buffer. `"
               & "io.put` buffers what fits, flushing first when it does n"
               & "ot, and writes a piece at least the buffer's size straig"
               & "ht through. `io.flush` writes with `write_some` until th"
               & "e buffer is empty, so after a failure exactly the unwrit"
               & "ten bytes stay at its front and a later flush writes eac"
               & "h byte once; a writer that makes no progress is `io_fail"
               & "ed`. Bytes still buffered when a program ends are never "
               & "written: `defer io.flush("
               & Character'Val (226)
               & Character'Val (128)
               & Character'Val (166)
               & ")` and a final flush whose failure is reported are the i"
               & "diom, documented as a hazard wherever the writer is. `io"
               & ".line_reader` lends each line until the next read, as a "
               & "directory lends its names (D293): a line ends at `\n`, a"
               & " `\r` before it belongs to the ending, a lone `\r` is a "
               & "byte, and the last line need not end. A line and its end"
               & "ing must fit the buffer; a longer one is `io.line_too_lo"
               & "ng` and is skipped, so the next read gives the following"
               & " line. End of input is a line marked `finished`, asked a"
               & "gain as often as the reader likes.",
            when 311 =>
               "Chosen: `_landin_host_initialize_arguments` takes C's th"
               & "ree `main` arguments, `(count: i32, escaping values: ptr"
               & " ptr u8, escaping environment: ptr ptr u8) -> none`, and"
               & " the hosted `main` passes its `envp` with the rest; it i"
               & "s already in the third argument register on every archit"
               & "ecture, so no backend moves anything. A null table is an"
               & " empty environment, and a repeat must repeat all three. "
               & "A static Linux program's entry passes the initial stack'"
               & "s table and the C runtime passes its own, so both reach "
               & "the environment through one routine. The table is counte"
               & "d again on every read, because C code may change it in p"
               & "lace.",
            when 312 =>
               "Chosen: `io.environment` is a concept outside `world`, w"
               & "ith `variable_count`, `variable_at` and `variable_named`"
               & ", the first match by bytes, failing `no_variable`. An `i"
               & "o.variable` is a name and a value, both host strings (D2"
               & "99), lent `from self`, which D301's static origin satisf"
               & "ies on a hosted system; an entry without `=` is a name w"
               & "ith an empty value. There is no setter: a program's own "
               & "environment is not changed beside threads, and a child g"
               & "ets the environment its parent builds. `io.variables_ove"
               & "r` gives a provider over `NAME=value` byte strings that "
               & "firmware can declare as static data.",
            when 313 =>
               "Chosen: `io.programs` is a concept outside `world`, shap"
               & "ed like D293. `io.spawn(host, path, arguments, environme"
               & "nt, streams)` runs the program at the path as given, wit"
               & "h no search and no shell; its first argument is the path"
               & ", and its environment exactly what the caller built. Eac"
               & "h of its three streams is `inherited`, `discarded` or `p"
               & "iped`, with presets `inheriting`, `capturing` and `disca"
               & "rding`. A running child is a value the caller edits: `io"
               & ".write_child` and `io.close_input` feed it, and `io.read"
               & "_child` waits on both piped outputs and reads whichever "
               & "is ready, so a child is never stalled on a full pipe. `i"
               & "o.wait` takes the child `sink`, closes its pipes and ans"
               & "wers `io.ending`, `exited(code)` or `signalled`; the sig"
               & "nal's number is hosted detail, `system.last_signal(host)"
               & "`, kept in a cell of the handle's `system.space` beside "
               & "its last error. `io.scripted_over(world, programs)` give"
               & "s scripted children whose output, errors, code and endin"
               & "g are given, recording how often each started, its argum"
               & "ent and variable counts and the input written to it.",
            when 314 =>
               "Chosen: `platform/posix` opens every descriptor close-on"
               & "-exec, files, directories and pipes. `posix.pipe` is `pi"
               & "pe2(O_CLOEXEC)` on Linux and FreeBSD and `pipe` followed"
               & " by `fcntl` on Darwin, which has no `pipe2`, so it is no"
               & "t atomic there. `posix.spawn` builds the argument and en"
               & "vironment tables in a temporary mapping and first moves "
               & "any stream descriptor below 3 that is not its own number"
               & " above 2. On Linux it is a `clone` with SIGCHLD and noth"
               & "ing shared, whose child sets its streams with `dup3`, cl"
               & "oses the rest with `close_range(3, ~0, CLOSE_RANGE_CLOEX"
               & "EC)` and calls `execve`; an exec failure reaches the par"
               & "ent through a close-on-exec pipe and the child is reaped"
               & ". On Darwin and FreeBSD it is `posix_spawn`, with `POSIX"
               & "_SPAWN_CLOEXEC_DEFAULT` and `posix_spawn_file_actions_ad"
               & "dinherit_np` on Darwin and `posix_spawn_file_actions_add"
               & "closefrom_np(3)` on FreeBSD. `posix.wait` is `wait4` or "
               & "`waitpid` and answers `exited(code)` or `signalled(signa"
               & "l)`; the hosted provider retries EINTR. A stream that is"
               & " already its own number is D378's, which amends this dec"
               & "ision.",
            when 378 =>
               "Chosen: `spawn` duplicates every stream below 3 above 2 "
               & "for the call, its own number included, with `F_DUPFD_CLO"
               & "EXEC`, and closes the duplicate after, so each stream re"
               & "aches its number in the child by a duplication from anot"
               & "her descriptor, which clears the close-on-exec flag in t"
               & "he child alone: `dup3(source, target, 0)` on Linux and `"
               & "posix_spawn_file_actions_adddup2` on Darwin and FreeBSD."
               & " The parent's descriptors and their flags are never chan"
               & "ged. The same descriptor may be given for several stream"
               & "s. A stream that is its own number and not open in the p"
               & "arent cannot be duplicated and is left as it is, so the "
               & "child's is not open either and the spawn goes on; any ot"
               & "her stream that is not open is `ebadf`. Darwin no longer"
               & " names an inherited stream: a stream that reaches the ch"
               & "ild is a duplication's target, which `POSIX_SPAWN_CLOEXE"
               & "C_DEFAULT` keeps. This amends D314.",
            when 315 =>
               "Chosen: `time.duration` and `time.instant` are each a `d"
               & "istinct u64` of nanoseconds, about 584 years, and ordere"
               & "d and compared as their base is (D302). `time.wall_time`"
               & " is a record of `seconds: i64` and `nanoseconds: u32`, U"
               & "TC since 1970 without leap seconds. Spans are made with "
               & "`time.nanoseconds`, `time.microseconds`, `time.milliseco"
               & "nds` and `time.seconds`, which trap past the range; `tim"
               & "e.elapsed` traps when its second reading is the earlier "
               & "one; `time.later` makes a deadline, and `time.in_millise"
               & "conds` rounds down. There is no other arithmetic on time"
               & ". Calendars, time zones and their formatting are the loc"
               & "ale record's in the roadmap's register.",
            when 316 =>
               "Chosen: `time.clock` holds `now` and `sleep` together, b"
               & "ecause a sleep is measured on that clock and its fake mu"
               & "st advance it; `time.wall_clock` holds `wall_now`, apart"
               & ", because firmware may count time without knowing the da"
               & "te and the wall clock jumps; `io.entropy` holds `fill_ra"
               & "ndom`. All three are outside `world`, with fakes in `cor"
               & "e/io`: `fake.clock_over` gives a `manual_clock` a test a"
               & "dvances, whose sleep advances it by exactly the span, an"
               & "d `fake.entropy_over` gives scripted bytes. Reading a cl"
               & "ock cannot fail; a failure of the system's own is `compi"
               & "ler.unreachable()`. A sleep cannot fail and never return"
               & "s before `now` has reached its start plus the span: the "
               & "hosted provider takes a deadline from the monotonic cloc"
               & "k and sleeps for what is left, at most a million seconds"
               & " a call, treating any failure, EINTR among them, as a re"
               & "ason to read the clock again; a deadline that would over"
               & "flow is the clock's last instant. Entropy is fallible, a"
               & "nd on Linux is `getrandom` with no flags, which waits on"
               & "ly before the kernel's pool is first ready, looping over"
               & " short reads and EINTR; on Darwin and FreeBSD it is `arc"
               & "4random_buf`, which cannot fail.",
            when 317 =>
               "Chosen: `platform/linux/vdso`'s `vdso.symbol` (D346) fin"
               & "ds the clock function the auxiliary vector's AT_SYSINFO_"
               & "EHDR names: `__vdso_clock_gettime` at `LINUX_2.6` on x86"
               & "-64, `__kernel_clock_gettime` at `LINUX_2.6.39` on arm64"
               & " and `__vdso_clock_gettime` at `LINUX_4.15` on RV64. It "
               & "reads the first load segment and the dynamic table, coun"
               & "ts symbols from `DT_HASH` or else `DT_GNU_HASH`, since o"
               & "nly x86 forces both, and requires the version, or the na"
               & "me alone where there are no version tables. Every offset"
               & " is held inside the image before it is read, by arithmet"
               & "ic that cannot overflow, and the image is bounded by its"
               & " first page for the headers and its first load segment, "
               & "at most a mebibyte. The function's address is cached in "
               & "a plain module word on first use, a relaxed `u64` cell o"
               & "f `core/atomic` since D502, and called through D335's co"
               & "nversion of that address to a C function value. A missin"
               & "g symbol, a malformed image or a nonzero answer falls ba"
               & "ck to the system call. Since D279's adoption it serves `"
               & "--link=libc` too, and `time.now` costs about 116 ns eith"
               & "er way.",
            when 318 =>
               "Chosen: `random.generator` is xoshiro256** 1.0 (Blackman"
               & " and Vigna, 2021), whose multiplications by 5 and 9 are "
               & "shifts and additions, so drawing needs no helper on Cort"
               & "ex-M0. `random.new(seed)` seeds it through splitmix64, a"
               & "s its authors advise; `random.from_entropy` reads 32 byt"
               & "es from an `io.entropy` provider and replaces the imposs"
               & "ible all-zero state with `new(0)`'s. `random.below` mask"
               & "s to the bound's width and draws again when the value is"
               & " too large, so it has neither division nor bias, and tra"
               & "ps on a bound of zero, with `overflow` since D342; `rand"
               & "om.shuffle` is Fisher and Yates'. A fixed seed's sequenc"
               & "e is the same on every target. It is not cryptographic, "
               & "as its documentation says.",
            when 319 =>
               "Chosen: `net.network` is a concept outside `world` that "
               & "also conforms to `reader` and `writer`, so a connection "
               & "is a `file` that `io.read`, `io.write`, the line reader "
               & "and the buffered writer take. Its entries are `connect`,"
               & " `listen`, `accept`, `open_datagram`, `send`, `receive`,"
               & " `send_to`, `receive_from`, `shutdown`, `local_address`,"
               & " `peer_address`, `set_timeouts`, `set_no_delay` and `clo"
               & "se_socket`. A system's errors become atoms: ECONNREFUSED"
               & " is `refused`; ENETUNREACH and EHOSTUNREACH `unreachable"
               & "`; EADDRINUSE `address_in_use`; EADDRNOTAVAIL, EAFNOSUPP"
               & "ORT and EPFNOSUPPORT `address_unavailable`; EACCES and E"
               & "PERM `no_access`; a limit passing, or ETIMEDOUT at conne"
               & "ct, `timed_out`; EPIPE, ECONNRESET, and ETIMEDOUT or ENO"
               & "TCONN on a connection, `disconnected`; anything else `io"
               & "_failed` with its errno kept. The calls block. `set_time"
               & "outs(receive, send)` sets limits, zero meaning none; a l"
               & "imit passing leaves the socket usable, and `accept` keep"
               & "s the receive limit on every system, by `poll` on Darwin"
               & " and FreeBSD. `connect` has no limit of its own. Every l"
               & "istener reuses its address and every IPv6 socket is IPv6"
               & " only, so an address names one family everywhere; the ba"
               & "cklog is 128. The hosted provider retries EINTR, waits o"
               & "ut an interrupted connect and reads its error, takes the"
               & " next connection after ECONNABORTED and sends until ever"
               & "y byte is sent.",
            when 320 =>
               "Chosen: `net.address` is a public record, as D293's dire"
               & "ctory is, so a provider in another module builds one, of"
               & " an `ipv4` or `ipv6` family, sixteen bytes and a port; i"
               & "t has no zone, so `%zone` is `invalid_address` and a lin"
               & "k-local address waits. IPv4 is four decimal parts with n"
               & "o leading zero, as `inet_pton` reads them. IPv6 is RFC 4"
               & "291's form in either case, with one `::` and an IPv4 tai"
               & "l; it is written as RFC 5952 says, in lower case with th"
               & "e longest run of two or more zero groups compressed, the"
               & " first on a tie, and only an IPv4-mapped address dotted."
               & " With a port it is `a.b.c.d:p` or `[v6]:p`. `net.parse_i"
               & "p`, `net.parse_address`, `net.append_ip` and `net.append"
               & "_address` read and write them, and an address is `format"
               & "table`.",
            when 321 =>
               "Chosen: `fake.network`, from `fake.network_over`, is one"
               & " machine with only loopback addresses, over socket recor"
               & "ds the caller declares, each record's buffer its receive"
               & " buffer. Delivery is at once, whole and in order; a data"
               & "gram no socket takes, or one its buffer has no room for,"
               & " is lost. It never waits: wherever a real call would, it"
               & " answers `timed_out` at once, after a send has delivered"
               & " what fits. A send to a closed peer is `disconnected` th"
               & "e first time. Ports are given from 49152, and a port ove"
               & "rlaps as on Linux, the unspecified address taking every "
               & "one. A test can turn IPv6 off, fail a chosen call and re"
               & "ad the counters. Resets, partial reads and TIME_WAIT are"
               & " not modelled. Its conformance links every entry, about "
               & "40 KB, so it does not fit a Cortex-M0 image.",
            when 322 =>
               "Chosen: the argument initializer ignores SIGPIPE on its "
               & "first call, and only when it finds the default dispositi"
               & "on, so a C `main`'s handler or an inherited ignore is ke"
               & "pt. That one place covers the static Linux entry, `--lin"
               & "k=libc`, Darwin, FreeBSD and a C `main`; a program that "
               & "imports no POSIX layer keeps the default. `posix.spawn` "
               & "gives every child the default again, on Linux in the clo"
               & "ne child before `execve` and elsewhere with `posix_spawn"
               & "attr_setsigdefault`. Every Linux send passes `MSG_NOSIGN"
               & "AL` and every Darwin and FreeBSD socket sets `SO_NOSIGPI"
               & "PE`, so socket writes are safe beside a C handler too, `"
               & "io.write` to a socket among them since D340; a pipe has "
               & "no such flag, so the process-wide ignore stays.",
            when 323 =>
               "Chosen: `posix.socket_address` is the system's own recor"
               & "d, laid out once per system: Linux's 16-bit family, and "
               & "Darwin's and FreeBSD's length byte and family byte. `pos"
               & "ix.socket` takes `internet`, `internet6` or `local` and "
               & "`stream` or `datagram`. Unix-domain sockets are this lay"
               & "er's alone, their paths at most 107 bytes on Linux and 1"
               & "03 on Darwin and FreeBSD, with empty, NUL-holding and ab"
               & "stract paths refused. Every socket is closed on exec, th"
               & "rough `SOCK_CLOEXEC` on Linux and FreeBSD and `fcntl` ri"
               & "ght after `socket` and `accept` on Darwin, which leaves "
               & "the same window as Darwin's pipes (D314). Its calls and "
               & "options are POSIX's own, and a timeout read back whose r"
               & "ecord has the wrong size is `unlisted` rather than trust"
               & "ed.",
            when 325 =>
               "Chosen: `io.file_system` is a concept outside `world` be"
               & "side `files` and `directories`, with `open_file`, `renam"
               & "e`, `status_of`, `status_of_file`, `set_read_only`, `syn"
               & "chronize`, `truncate`, `read_at`, `write_at`, `make_temp"
               & "orary` and `current_directory`. Opening takes an `open_o"
               & "ptions` record of `read`, `write`, `append`, `create`, `"
               & "exclusive` and `truncate`, with presets `updating`, `app"
               & "ending` and `creating`; an impossible combination is `io"
               & "_failed`, EINVAL kept, before the system is asked. `rena"
               & "me` replaces a taken name in one step, as POSIX and Wind"
               & "ows' replacing move do; ENOENT is `not_found`, EACCES, E"
               & "PERM and EROFS `no_access`, and everything else, EXDEV a"
               & "nd ENOTDIR among them, `io_failed` with its errno, since"
               & " rename's ENOTDIR also means a directory onto a file and"
               & " D287 does not apply. `io.status` is a size, an `entry_k"
               & "ind`, a modification `wall_time` and `read_only`, which "
               & "means no permission bit lets anyone write; `set_read_onl"
               & "y(false)` restores the owner's write bit alone, in two c"
               & "alls. `synchronize(data_only)` is `fsync` or `fdatasync`"
               & ", and on Darwin `F_FULLFSYNC`, falling back to `fsync` w"
               & "here a file system refuses it. `truncate` takes an open "
               & "file only. `read_at` may return short and returns zero a"
               & "t or past the end; `write_at` writes everything, leaving"
               & " a hole of zeros past the end; writing at an offset to a"
               & " file opened for appending is a documented hazard, since"
               & " Linux ignores the offset there. The working directory c"
               & "an be read and is never changed, since it is process-wid"
               & "e state beside threads. `io.terminals` is a second conce"
               & "pt, whether a stream is a terminal and its window size, "
               & "failing `not_a_terminal`. The fakes are `fake.volume`, a"
               & " node-based volume for all five file concepts, which doe"
               & "s not fit Cortex-M0 because its conformances link every "
               & "entry, and `fake.terminals`.",
            when 326 =>
               "Chosen: `io.make_temporary(host, names, directory, buffe"
               & "r)` creates `.tmp-` and sixteen hexadecimal digits in a "
               & "directory, exclusively, close on exec and with mode 0600"
               & ", the digits drawn from the `io.entropy` source given as"
               & " `names`; a taken name is tried again up to sixteen time"
               & "s, then `io_failed` with EEXIST kept. Nothing removes th"
               & "e file: the caller renames it into place or removes it. "
               & "The result names the file `from` the caller's buffer.",
            when 327 =>
               "Chosen: every open in the POSIX layer is `O_NOCTTY`, so "
               & "opening a terminal never makes it the controlling one. `"
               & "posix.status` gains permission bits, a link count, a `us"
               & "er_id`, a `group_id` and three times. `link_at` never fo"
               & "llows the old name's last link, and `read_link_at` fails"
               & " `erange` when the target fills the buffer. `change_mode"
               & "(_at)` follows links, since Linux's `fchmodat` cannot do"
               & " otherwise, and refuses bits above 0o7777; `change_owner"
               & "(_at)` and `set_times(_at)` take a `follow` flag, and ti"
               & "mes are always both given. Both kinds of lock every syst"
               & "em has are offered: `lock` and `unlock`, `flock`'s, whol"
               & "e-file and owned by the open file, and `lock_range` and "
               & "`unlock_range`, POSIX record locks owned by the process,"
               & " not inherited by a child and all dropped when any descr"
               & "iptor of the file is closed, a hazard documented and pin"
               & "ned. A refused lock is `eagain`, or `eacces` for a recor"
               & "d lock, and the documentation advises one kind per file.",
            when 328 =>
               "Chosen: `posix.terminal_mode` wraps each system's own re"
               & "cord, the kernel's `termios` through `ioctl` on Linux, n"
               & "ever the C library's, and `tcgetattr` on Darwin and Free"
               & "BSD. `posix.raw_mode` applies `cfmakeraw`'s flags, and r"
               & "estoring the mode is the caller's, with `defer`. `posix."
               & "open_pseudo_terminal` opens `/dev/ptmx` and asks `TIOCGP"
               & "TPEER` on Linux, falling back to `/dev/pts/N`, and uses "
               & "`posix_openpt`, `grantpt`, `unlockpt` and `ptsname_r` el"
               & "sewhere, both ends closed on exec.",
            when 329 =>
               "Chosen: the fixed fact `compiler.c_runtime` is true on D"
               & "arwin and FreeBSD, true on Linux only under `--link=libc"
               & "`, and false otherwise. On a C runtime the account and g"
               & "roup lookups use the `get*_r` calls, which ask NSS or th"
               & "e directory service; a static Linux program reads `/etc/"
               & "passwd` and `/etc/group` itself, a line at a time in the"
               & " caller's buffer, taking the first match, so accounts ke"
               & "pt elsewhere need `--link=libc`. A comment, a NIS `+` or"
               & " `-` line, a line with the wrong number of fields, an em"
               & "pty name or an identifier that is not a decimal below 0x"
               & "FFFFFFFF is no entry; a line too long for the buffer is "
               & "skipped, and if nothing matched after one the answer is "
               & "`erange`; empty member names are skipped. On the C route"
               & " a missing entry, or ENOENT, ESRCH, EBADF or EPERM with "
               & "none, is `no_account`.",
            when 330 =>
               "Chosen: a call-site `else` followed by a parenthesised n"
               & "ame or `_`, and not by `:=`, opens that call's recovery "
               & "wherever it stands, an `if` arm included. Any other call"
               & "-site `else` divides the `if` where it can close a `then"
               & "` or `elsif` arm, so `if c then a() else b() end if` kee"
               & "ps its one-line meaning, and `(f() else 0)` recovers the"
               & " call there; the refusals of that form name the route. `"
               & "if c then f() else (r) end if` is refused with an exact "
               & "fix to `else r`, since parentheses after a call's `else`"
               & " bind its error. A recovery's body starts its own arm.",
            when 331 =>
               "Chosen: a `(` that begins a line, and whose matching `)`"
               & " is followed by `:=`, begins a destructuring binding. Co"
               & "ntinuation is otherwise unchanged, so a call's arguments"
               & " and a conformance's entries may still begin the next li"
               & "ne. The parser records where a line-leading `(` or prefi"
               & "x operator continued a line, and a later refusal there s"
               & "ays so: a construction after a name is L0301 naming `siz"
               & "e(rows: 0, "
               & Character'Val (226)
               & Character'Val (128)
               & Character'Val (166)
               & ")` as the route, without the misleading report that used"
               & " to come first; an undeclared name and a value that beca"
               & "me an operand say the line above was continued.",
            when 332 =>
               "Chosen: `declared_type ::= type | atom_union` is the typ"
               & "e of a binding, a condition declaration, a parameter, a "
               & "named return and a field, payload fields included; `ptr "
               & "a | b` is the pointer union of `ptr a` and `b`. It is th"
               & "e same structural set an alias with those members names "
               & "(D216). As an element type, a type argument, a labelled "
               & "argument, a `distinct` or range base, a conformance targ"
               & "et, a static type argument or `sizeof`'s operand it is s"
               & "till refused, once, naming the alias.",
            when 333 =>
               "Chosen: `lenof` takes a name, a field or element path, a"
               & " slice, a call's result or a literal. A name, or a path "
               & "that names a fixed array, is measured from its type and "
               & "not read, nor any index inside it, though a constant ind"
               & "ex is still checked; so `lenof rows[i]` over a fixed arr"
               & "ay does not evaluate `i`. A slice is evaluated once, and"
               & " a call is always evaluated, even when it returns a fixe"
               & "d array. Indexing or selecting a call's result stays [18"
               & "30]'s recorded boundary, and L0010 says to bind the valu"
               & "e to a name and index the name; a `[` beginning the line"
               & " after a call is no longer read as an index.",
            when 334 =>
               "Chosen: a branch of a statement `if`, `elsif` or `else` "
               & "arm, a statement `match` arm or a bare `begin` that ends"
               & " with a value is L0331, as D244 refuses a call standing "
               & "alone that hands back a result, naming both routes: the "
               & "branch written as a statement, or the call's recovery pa"
               & "renthesised or bound. A recovery's own block stays D310'"
               & "s.",
            when 335 =>
               "Chosen: a C function type applied to one `usize`, writte"
               & "n in place or through an alias, `adder(address)`, makes "
               & "a C function value of the code at that address. Nothing "
               & "can check that code of that signature is there; that is "
               & "the program's, as a C cast is. The bits are unchanged. Z"
               & "ero traps where the value is made, inside `unchecked` to"
               & "o, and a known zero is refused with L0335. The address c"
               & "arries no origin [0810]. A native function type applied "
               & "to an address is L0301, since Landin's own convention is"
               & " no ABI, and so is an integer of another type or a point"
               & "er, which `usize(p)` converts first. Nothing converts a "
               & "function value back to an address. The conversion is the"
               & " IR's `code_address`, a move on every backend.",
            when 336 =>
               "Chosen: `posix.open_library(path, scope)` loads a C libr"
               & "ary with `RTLD_NOW` and an explicit `local_symbols` or `"
               & "global_symbols`, since Darwin's default scope is global "
               & "and the others' local, wherever the system's loader star"
               & "ted the process: on Darwin and FreeBSD always, and on Li"
               & "nux under `--link=libc`, where glibc 2.34 or musl provid"
               & "e the loader in the C library. A `library` is an opaque "
               & "handle passed by value, as D288 has services, since the "
               & "loader counts the opens and two loads of one object give"
               & " the same handle; it cannot be zeroed into being. `posix"
               & ".find_symbol` gives an address, which D335 makes a typed"
               & " function value. Loading fails with an `errno` atom or `"
               & "no_library`, a lookup with `no_symbol`, closing with `no"
               & "_library`; the loader's own words are opt-in, `posix.lib"
               & "rary_failure(into)` copying `dlerror`'s text into the ca"
               & "ller's buffer, cut to fit, read at once on the same thre"
               & "ad. A function value has no origin (D113), so one from a"
               & " closed library dangles, as a pointer after `free` does,"
               & " and the documentation says so. A static Linux program t"
               & "hat reaches these calls is refused by D280's L0500, nami"
               & "ng the routines that ask for the C library. Code loaded "
               & "so is C, or Landin only through C entry points.",
            when 337 =>
               "Chosen: `mem.allocator` has a fourth entry, `resize(self"
               & ", block, old_size, new_size, alignment) -> (moved: ptr m"
               & "ut u8) ! out_of_memory`, and `mem.resize` calls it. The "
               & "result holds the block's first `min(old_size, new_size)`"
               & " bytes, honours the same alignment and is freed with `ne"
               & "w_size`; when it moved, the old address is given back. A"
               & " refusal leaves the block, its bytes and the provider as"
               & " they were. A concept entry has no default, so the defau"
               & "lt is a function: `mem.relocate` allocates, copies and f"
               & "rees through the provider, and a provider that cannot re"
               & "size in place calls it from its own entry once any in-pl"
               & "ace change has been refused. The arena keeps a smaller b"
               & "lock where it is, gives the latest block's tail back, gr"
               & "ows the latest block in place and moves any other; a poo"
               & "l keeps a block in its slot to any extent the slot holds"
               & " and refuses a larger one; an injector spends its budget"
               & " on a resize as on an allocation and delegates it; and a"
               & " region resizes the block its newest record holds throug"
               & "h its parent, updating the record, and moves any other i"
               & "nto a record of its own, the old one freed at `release` "
               & "as a freed block is. The hosted heap resizes in place wh"
               & "en the block's slot or mapping holds the new extent, giv"
               & "ing a shrunk mapping's whole pages back, and otherwise g"
               & "rows a mapping where the pages after it are free; on Lin"
               & "ux `posix.remap`, `mremap` with `MREMAP_MAYMOVE`, moves "
               & "its pages when they are not, provided a page has the blo"
               & "ck's alignment, and anything else is copied by `mem.relo"
               & "cate`. Darwin and FreeBSD have no `mremap`: `posix.exten"
               & "d` asks for the pages after the mapping without `MAP_FIX"
               & "ED` and keeps them only where the system put them. Its `"
               & "grow` now extends in place by the same means. `text.grow"
               & "ing` doubles through `resize`.",
            when 340 =>
               "Chosen: a socket the hosted provider makes carries a mar"
               & "k beside its descriptor in the `io.file` it gives, a bit"
               & " no descriptor has, and `io.write` and `write_some` send"
               & " on a marked file, where `posix.send` passes `MSG_NOSIGN"
               & "AL` on Linux and Darwin and FreeBSD's sockets carry `SO_"
               & "NOSIGPIPE`. `system.descriptor_of` drops the mark. `syst"
               & "em.socket_of` makes such a file from a socket `platform/"
               & "posix` made; `file_of` keeps making a plain one, whose w"
               & "rites are POSIX's `write`, as its documentation now says"
               & ".",
            when 341 =>
               "Chosen: the volume resolves every path as a system does,"
               & " part by part: a link before the last part is always fol"
               & "lowed, the last as the call says, a target beginning wit"
               & "h `/` from the root and any other from the link's own di"
               & "rectory, `..` climbing from where the walk has reached. "
               & "A part before the last that is missing or no directory i"
               & "s `not_found`, more than eight links `io_failed` as ELOO"
               & "P is, and a path that grows past 256 bytes as targets ar"
               & "e put in it `io_failed`. A creating open of a dangling l"
               & "ink makes its target, and an exclusive one is `already_e"
               & "xists`, as O_EXCL is. Removing works on the link itself;"
               & " a directory asked of anything else is `not_found`, a fi"
               & "le asked of a directory `io_failed`, as Linux's EISDIR i"
               & "s. The memory network's listener conflicts only with lis"
               & "teners, while a connection's port still conflicts with b"
               & "oth. A line reader over an empty buffer reports every li"
               & "ne `line_too_long` and never reads.",
            when 380 =>
               "Chosen: every call of the volume's `reader`, `writer`, `"
               & "files`, `directories` and `file_system` counts once in `"
               & "calls`, `read_entry`, `entry_size` and `same_file` among"
               & " them, and the call `fail_at` names fails `io_failed`. T"
               & "wo compose others and count what they make: `write` coun"
               & "ts each piece `write_some` writes, and `make_temporary` "
               & "counts itself and each name it tries to open. A read fai"
               & "ls before it touches the directory, so the next one give"
               & "s the entry the failed one would have. The hosted provid"
               & "er can fail each of these calls: a read that refills cal"
               & "ls `getdents` or `readdir`, one that does not may stat a"
               & "n entry whose record gives no kind, and `entry_size` and"
               & " `same_file` each stat.",
            when 342 =>
               "Chosen: `random.below(source, 0)` traps with `overflow`,"
               & " at the checked subtraction that makes its mask, as `n %"
               & " 0` traps: the bound is the remainder's divisor that a b"
               & "iased `next % bound` would have used. D318's other choic"
               & "es stand. `next_u32`'s documentation gives xoshiro256**'"
               & "s own reason for the upper half: every bit of its output"
               & " passes its authors' tests, so the half is a convention,"
               & " where the low bits of xoshiro256+ are the weak ones.",
            when 343 =>
               "Chosen: on Darwin and FreeBSD `read`, `write`, `read_at`"
               & " and `write_at` ask for at most INT_MAX bytes and return"
               & " short past it. `open_library` of an empty path is `enoe"
               & "nt`, as every other call of the module answers one. `lin"
               & "ux.poll_limit` is `no_limit | ptr mut timespec`. FreeBSD"
               & "'s `posix_openpt` is asked for O_CLOEXEC; Darwin's docum"
               & "ents only O_RDWR and O_NOCTTY and keeps the `fcntl`. Eac"
               & "h `file_status` record is chosen by its system and C ABI"
               & " by name, and a system none names has none.",
            when 344 =>
               "Chosen: a name longer than 255 bytes, Linux's LOGIN_NAME"
               & "_MAX without its NUL and the largest of the three system"
               & "s', names no one on both routes, and a missing database "
               & "file is `no_account`. The C group lookup gives the C lib"
               & "rary the caller's whole buffer, measures the copy the jo"
               & "ined members need, and asks again into the part of the b"
               & "uffer past that copy, so a group is `erange` only when i"
               & "t and its copy together do not fit; a group that grew be"
               & "tween the two lookups is `erange` too.",
            when 345 =>
               "Chosen: `vec.list` is a public name for a module-interna"
               & "l record, so its field is unreachable outside `core/vec`"
               & ", as `spill.list`'s storage already was. The heap's docu"
               & "mentation states that `free` frees the extent its header"
               & " holds, never reads the size passed, and is undefined fo"
               & "r a block it did not give or one freed twice, as C's `fr"
               & "ee` is; and that a refused unmap keeps the pages, which "
               & "costs memory and nothing else.",
            when 346 =>
               "Chosen: `platform/posix` is one file per facility, `posi"
               & "x.ldn` for the descriptor, paths and the module's shared"
               & " helpers, then `files.ldn`, `directories.ldn`, `memory.l"
               & "dn`, `time.ldn`, `random.ldn`, `poll.ldn`, `processes.ld"
               & "n`, `sockets.ldn`, `terminals.ldn`, `accounts.ldn`, `lib"
               & "raries.ldn` and `errno.ldn`. Each holds its facility's i"
               & "nterface and, beneath it, the system's calls in one `fix"
               & "ed if compiler.os == linux` and one `elsif compiler.os ="
               & "= darwin or compiler.os == freebsd`, so each route is na"
               & "med by what selects it and lies beside what it serves. `"
               & "platform/libc` keeps in `libc.ldn` what every system dec"
               & "lares alike, and gives Linux, Darwin and FreeBSD each a "
               & "file of its own, `linux.ldn`, `darwin.ldn` and `freebsd."
               & "ldn`, wholly under its own `fixed if`; a declaration two"
               & " systems share is written in each. `malloc`, `free`, `al"
               & "location` and `no_allocation` are removed. The vDSO, whi"
               & "ch only a caller reading a clock needs, is `platform/lin"
               & "ux/vdso`, a submodule as `platform/linux/numbers` is, an"
               & "d its names lose the prefix the module now gives them: `"
               & "vdso.kernel_image`, `vdso.find`, `vdso.symbol`, `vdso.cl"
               & "ock_symbol`, `vdso.clock_version`, `vdso.clock_gettime`,"
               & " `vdso.largest` and `vdso.at_sysinfo_ehdr`. No other pub"
               & "lic name changes.",
            when 347 =>
               "Chosen: the module is `hosted/system`, imported with no "
               & "alias. Its handle's type is `system.host`, made by `syst"
               & "em.new()`, or from a `system.space` by `system.over`; `s"
               & "ystem.last_errno`, `last_signal`, `descriptor_of`, `file"
               & "_of` and `socket_of` keep their names. The heap's type i"
               & "s `heap.heap`, made by `heap.new()`. So `system` names t"
               & "he module, `host` the I/O handle and its parameter, and "
               & "`heap` the allocator, each one thing in both layers. The"
               & " module's files mirror `core/io`'s: `system.ldn` for the"
               & " four concepts of `world` and the environment, `director"
               & "ies.ldn`, `file_system.ldn` with terminals as `core/io` "
               & "keeps them, `time.ldn`, `entropy.ldn`, `network.ldn` and"
               & " `programs.ldn`.",
            when 348 =>
               "Chosen: `core/time` holds `duration`, `instant`, `wall_t"
               & "ime`, the `clock` and `wall_clock` concepts and their ar"
               & "ithmetic; `core/net` holds the `network` concept, which "
               & "refines `io.reader` and `io.writer`, its addresses and i"
               & "ts atoms; `core/io` keeps the files, the process, the en"
               & "vironment, directories, programs, the file system, termi"
               & "nals, entropy, the buffered writer and the line reader, "
               & "and its status stamps a `time.wall_time`. The fakes of a"
               & " system are the submodule `core/io/fake`, named one way:"
               & " a provider type for what it fakes, its caller-owned sta"
               & "te that type with `_space`, and its constructor that typ"
               & "e with `_over`: `fake.volume`, `volume_space`, `volume_o"
               & "ver`; `fake.network`, `network_space`, `network_over`; `"
               & "fake.clock`, `clock_space`, `clock_over`; `fake.entropy`"
               & ", `entropy_space`, `entropy_over`; and `fake.terminals` "
               & "with `terminals_over`. The caller's records keep their p"
               & "rovider's name, `fake.volume_node`, `fake.network_socket"
               & "` and `fake.screen`, since a record named `socket` would"
               & " take a name every routine gives a parameter. The memory"
               & " world, `io.memory`, stays in `core/io` with its environ"
               & "ment and its scripted programs, which write into the wor"
               & "ld's own streams: it is firmware's own world rather than"
               & " a fake of a system's, and it is what makes `io.writer_o"
               & "f`, an erased `any world`, dispatchable in every program"
               & " that imports `core/io`, since a closed program refuses "
               & "an erased call no conformance can answer (D145). A depen"
               & "dency runs one way: `core/net` and `core/io/fake` import"
               & " `core/io`, and `core/io` imports `core/time`. No behavi"
               & "our changes.",
            when 349 =>
               "Chosen: the module is `platform/cortex_m`, imported as `"
               & "cortex_m`, with its routines unchanged: `cortex_m.disabl"
               & "e_interrupts`, `restore_interrupts`, `interrupt_mask`, `"
               & "wait_for_interrupt`, `device_barrier`, `completion_barri"
               & "er` and `compiler_barrier`. Namespace availability refus"
               & "es it off an M-profile target by its new name, and a mod"
               & "ule for another profile is named for that profile in tur"
               & "n.",
            when 350 =>
               "Chosen: the memory network's role is the private atom se"
               & "t `free_slot | listening_slot | connection_slot | datagr"
               & "am_slot`; a scripted program holds an `io.ending`, `(how"
               & ": io.exited(code: 3))` or `(how: io.signalled)`, as `wai"
               & "t` reports it; a `child_read` has a `stream`, `io.child_"
               & "output` or `io.child_errors`, of the type `io.child_stre"
               & "am`; the builder's buffer is `not_allocated` or `allocat"
               & "ed`; `io.status_of` takes an `io.link_handling`, `io.fol"
               & "lowing` or `io.not_following`, and `io.synchronize` an `"
               & "io.synchronizing`, `io.data_and_status` or `io.data_only"
               & "`. The counters are `reads`, `writes`, `opens`, `closes`"
               & " and `losses`. `platform/posix` keeps POSIX's own flags,"
               & " where a bool is the system's interface. The region's le"
               & "dger of capacity zero, which grows, and the pool's vacan"
               & "t slot, a `size` of the largest `usize`, keep their enco"
               & "dings for now, since each is a fixed parameter or a reco"
               & "rd callers initialise, and their change waits for the re"
               & "ading of those modules.",
            when 351 =>
               "Chosen: a byte that is a character is written `u8('c')`,"
               & " D199's checked conversion of the character literal, whi"
               & "ch a constant folds; `u8('\n')` for a line end. The libr"
               & "ary and the corpus write every byte they compare or appe"
               & "nd as text so, and keep numbers where a byte is a number"
               & ": a record's kind byte, an octet of an address, NUL as `"
               & "0`. D163 is unchanged.",
            when 352 =>
               "Chosen: `cmp.compare`, `cmp.less`, `cmp.equal`, `cmp.gre"
               & "ater` and `cmp.order` replace `core/mem`'s, unchanged in"
               & " meaning, and `[]u8 is ordered` with `compare`'s `less`."
               & " `core/mem` keeps copying, filling and finding bytes. `c"
               & "ore/cmp` still imports nothing, so every module can impo"
               & "rt it.",
            when 353 =>
               "Chosen: `hosted/system` has one `path_failure`, which ke"
               & "eps the errno and fails as the concepts say of a path, a"
               & "nd one `open`, which takes the options and the creation "
               & "mode, retries EINTR and gives `already_exists` for a tak"
               & "en exclusive name; every open of every concept and `make"
               & "_temporary` call it, the latter now retrying an interrup"
               & "ted attempt in place rather than spending one of its tri"
               & "es. `platform/posix` has one `forgotten`. No interface o"
               & "r behaviour changes, but that interrupted temporary atte"
               & "mpt. `platform/posix`'s `/etc/passwd` and `/etc/group` p"
               & "arsers stay public for now: `runtime/posix-accounts` hol"
               & "ds every malformed-line refusal through them, and the st"
               & "atic route reads the system's own files, which a test ca"
               & "nnot replace.",
            when 354 =>
               "Chosen: changed: a tree node says what it is, `tree.kind"
               & "` of `tree.leaf_node | tree.branch_node`, how many leave"
               & "s it counts, `tree.leaves`, and which nodes are its chil"
               & "dren, `tree.children`, and the module keeps its name, si"
               & "nce an append-only tree of named nodes is a tree; a spil"
               & "l list has `spill.clear`, `spill.last` and `spill.reserv"
               & "e`, and its storage is the module's own as `vec.list`'s "
               & "is (D345); a bounded diagnostic entry lends its whole me"
               & "ssage, `diag.message`; an arena gives every allocation b"
               & "ack at once, `mem.arena_reset`; a region grows the block"
               & " its newest record holds in place through its parent, an"
               & "d `mem.grow` makes the allocator's `grow` callable as `m"
               & "em.resize` makes `resize`; the memory file's `opened` an"
               & "d `writing` are one `state`, `io.closed_slot`, `io.readi"
               & "ng_slot` or `io.writing_slot`; `host()` is `new()` (D347"
               & "); and byte strings are ordered (D352). Kept, each for i"
               & "ts reason: `io.argument_at` takes the handle by value as"
               & " `out` and `err` do since D288, so that point no longer "
               & "stands; the map's representation is the module's own, a "
               & "public alias of a private record, with `map.removed` cou"
               & "nting the dead entries a caller read from it before, and"
               & " `map.cursor`'s slot private too; a private alias of a t"
               & "ype whose formal carries a constraint first stopped the "
               & "checker with an internal defect, since a template is che"
               & "cked once with its formals symbolic and the constraint w"
               & "as asked of the symbolic type, which is now left to each"
               & " concrete application; the compositions `runtime/r420-ma"
               & "p-operations` built below the map, a seven-slot table an"
               & "d forged buckets, cannot be made and are gone with the p"
               & "ublic composition; a saved PRIMASK stays a `u32`, since "
               & "every bit but one is reserved and the value is only ever"
               & " restored or counted, which a distinct type would make l"
               & "onger to write and no safer; `text.nowhere` waits for th"
               & "e text cursor's retirement, which removes it; `pool.over"
               & "`'s misconfiguration, `grow_storage`'s three extents and"
               & " the fault injector's refusal to grow in place wait for "
               & "the readings of those modules, the last because a dozen "
               & "fixtures pin which path a container takes through an inj"
               & "ector by its counters.",
            when 355 =>
               "Chosen: the slice writers and `text.prefix` are retired;"
               & " the builder's `append_u32`, `append_u64` and `append_us"
               & "ize` are the library's one decimal writer, private at ea"
               & "ch width so that a 32-bit image divides in 32 bits, as D"
               & "286 chose. Every `parse_*` and `to_u32` is `numbers.ldn`"
               & "'s, written over one scanner per width, and `core/net` r"
               & "eads an address's parts with `text.parse_u8` and `text.p"
               & "arse_hex_u32`. `io.format(writer, template, values)` for"
               & "mats straight into a buffered writer's buffer: into the "
               & "room after what waits, after a flush when the text does "
               & "not fit there, and refused whole with `text.no_space` wh"
               & "en it is larger than the buffer; the builder and the buf"
               & "fered writer are the byte sinks a template is formatted "
               & "into. `core/text`'s cursor, `text.position`, stays, and "
               & "with it `text.nowhere`: D182 makes `utf8[position]` the "
               & "language's direct byte-offset index, which reads that ex"
               & "act type, so retiring the cursor is a language change an"
               & "d is left to one.",
            when 356 =>
               "Chosen: `mem.storage_extent`, `mem.reserve_storage` and "
               & "`mem.release_storage` are the containers' one way of tak"
               & "ing and giving back slots: a reserve grows the block in "
               & "place where the provider does and moves it otherwise, pu"
               & "blished last; `grow_storage` is private, so no caller pa"
               & "sses its extents. The injector delegates `grow`, spendin"
               & "g its budget on the attempt, and counts a growth in plac"
               & "e as `fault.growths`, so `successes` is still the blocks"
               & " it gave and each is freed once; every fixture that pinn"
               & "ed an injector's counters was rewritten for a growth ask"
               & "ed before an allocation, holding what is the same whiche"
               & "ver way a provider answers where the answer depends on t"
               & "he system's pages. `region.growing_space` names the grow"
               & "ing ledger, which capacity zero still is, since a bounde"
               & "d ledger of no records could hold nothing. Two parts wer"
               & "e stopped on inspection. The arena stays in `core/mem`: "
               & "as a module of its own it would leave every program that"
               & " imports `core/text`, whose growing builder is an `any m"
               & "em.allocator`, with no allocator conformance, which D145"
               & " refuses (L0342) though no such value could exist, so mo"
               & "ving it waits on that rule. The pool's vacant slot stays"
               & " the largest `usize`: `runtime/r420-pool-provider` pins "
               & "the slot's sixteen bytes against the padded form with a "
               & "flag, and callers declare the slots `zeroed`, which no a"
               & "tom set can be (L0328).",
            when 357 =>
               "Chosen: `file_system` refines `files`, so its providers "
               & "open with `open_read`, `open_write` and `open_file` and "
               & "close each with `files`' `close`. L0201 for a member the"
               & " module declares only in a `fixed if` arm this target do"
               & "es not select says that the module declares it only for "
               & "another target. A template is checked once with its type"
               & " formals symbolic, and a constraint asked of a symbolic "
               & "formal inside an alias's body is now left to the alias's"
               & " concrete applications, which normalize the body again a"
               & "nd refuse a type without the evidence there. The memory "
               & "world is not rebuilt over the volume: the volume's confo"
               & "rmance tables link every entry of five concepts, about 1"
               & "00 KiB, which a firmware image over the memory world, th"
               & "e world it is kept in `core/io` for, cannot hold in its "
               & "32 KiB.",
            when 386 =>
               "Chosen: the pool's `grow` keeps the block in its slot to"
               & " any extent the slot holds and records that extent for t"
               & "he block's free, as `resize` does, and refuses a larger "
               & "extent, a block that is not a live slot of `old_size` an"
               & "d an address inside a slot rather than at it, with the p"
               & "ool unchanged. The block does not move, so it keeps the "
               & "alignment it was allocated with. `free`, `grow` and `res"
               & "ize` find their slot through one private routine, so the"
               & "y refuse alike, and `resize` is a growth or shrink in pl"
               & "ace. No slot is larger than another, so a growth past th"
               & "e slot finds nowhere to go, and `mem.reserve_storage`'s "
               & "fresh allocation is refused as before. Every Cortex-M0 i"
               & "mage over a pool that the corpus runs is smaller than it"
               & " was. The fixtures that counted a second slot for a grow"
               & "th now count one allocation and hold the refusal past th"
               & "e slot instead.",
            when 387 =>
               "Chosen: `sort.sort_by(values, by, less)` sorts with `les"
               & "s: (by: context, left: item, right: item) -> (yes: bool)"
               & "`, generic over `item` and `context`, and passes `by` to"
               & " every comparison unchanged. A context is any value: a s"
               & "lice of the shared storage, a record holding one, or a p"
               & "ointer through which the comparison counts or caches. It"
               & " is the same heapsort as `sort`, with no allocation, con"
               & "stant storage and bounded depth, and the comparison must"
               & " be a strict weak ordering while it runs. A context whos"
               & "e type disagrees with the comparison's is D138's L0340. "
               & "`sort` and `sort_selection` are unchanged, so no image t"
               & "hat sorts by evidence grows.",
            when 388 =>
               "Chosen: `core/failure` is a shared freestanding module o"
               & "f one type and one routine. `failure.reason` is the unio"
               & "n of every atom a `core` module fails with, thirty-two o"
               & "f them from `core/mem`, `core/map`, `core/tree`, `core/i"
               & "o`, `core/net` and `core/text`, and `failure.words(probl"
               & "em)` returns a fixed phrase for each: lower case with no"
               & " final stop, so that it reads after a subject and a colo"
               & "n, static text that borrows nothing, the same on every t"
               & "arget and in every locale. A call's failure set widens t"
               & "o `failure.reason` whatever subset of it the call declar"
               & "es, so `else (problem)` passes it straight on. A set tha"
               & "t also holds the program's own atom does not widen, so a"
               & " `match` names the program's atoms and passes the rest o"
               & "n through D434's `_ (rest):` binding, which holds only t"
               & "he library's; the subject itself still does not widen, a"
               & "nd that refusal is [0640]'s L0301. Atoms that are values"
               & " rather than failures, a directory entry's kind or an or"
               & "der, have no words, and `platform/posix`'s errno detail "
               & "stays with its provider (D207). A program that never cal"
               & "ls `words` links none of it (D296); one that does carrie"
               & "s every phrase, about 6 KB on Cortex-M0, which a `match`"
               & " of thirty-two arms costs there.",
            when 418 =>
               "Chosen: under D415 a public routine is a local symbol, s"
               & "o it can replace nothing, and the prefixes are dropped: "
               & "174 link names go, and each routine keeps its own name, "
               & "which a debugger and a backtrace now show. No C peer, C "
               & "runtime or assembly block called any of them by a prefix"
               & "ed name. The two symbols the C runtime and the kernel do"
               & " reach keep theirs: the process entry `_landin_start` an"
               & "d `_landin_host_initialize_arguments`, which a C-owned `"
               & "main` calls. `_landin_start_main` stays a public C defin"
               & "ition, which `_landin_start` calls from its assembly blo"
               & "ck.",
            when 425 =>
               "Chosen: `vec.list(u8)` is the growable byte container, w"
               & "ith three operations over it. `vec.append_bytes` copies "
               & "a slice after the bytes the list holds; `vec.spare_bytes"
               & "` lends the spare capacity past them, at least the bytes"
               & " asked for, as the buffer a read fills; and `vec.extend_"
               & "bytes` counts the bytes written there as appended. The f"
               & "irst two grow the list as `push` does, doubling, or to e"
               & "xactly what is asked when doubling is not enough, and re"
               & "port `mem.out_of_memory` changing nothing; counting more"
               & " than the spare capacity is `mem.out_of_bounds`, also ch"
               & "anging nothing. Beneath them `core/mem` gives the byte s"
               & "torage the same three: `spare_bytes`, `admit_bytes` and "
               & "`admit_copy`, the last failing with `full`. The spare ca"
               & "pacity holds whatever the backing held, which every byte"
               & " value is, so the view is only for bytes: a spare slot o"
               & "f another item type could hold no value of it, an atom s"
               & "et's among them. The copy is `mem.copy`, a word at a tim"
               & "e where it moves words and a byte at a time on firmware,"
               & " and so is the move when the list grows: `mem.transfer_p"
               & "refix`, which `mem.reserve_storage` moves a block's item"
               & "s with when the provider cannot grow it in place, copies"
               & " their bytes whole rather than a typed transfer per item"
               & ", and D356's protocol, a growth asked in place before an"
               & " allocation, stays as it was. Reading reverse-complement"
               & "'s input on Linux x86-64 at `--optimize speed` into a li"
               & "st through `spare_bytes` takes 0.40 seconds, and 0.44 th"
               & "rough `append_bytes` from a 64 KiB buffer, against 2.5 t"
               & "o 3.7 with the reserve moving items one at a time and 0."
               & "23 through `core/text`'s growing builder, whose `resize`"
               & " lets `hosted/heap` move a large block's pages rather th"
               & "an copy them. Reverse-complement keeps the builder: thro"
               & "ugh a list it took 0.94 seconds against the builder's 0."
               & "79.",
            when 442 =>
               "Chosen: they keep `ptr u8`. Their caller is `platform/po"
               & "six`, which copies a host string into a room, ends it wi"
               & "th NUL and passes `terminate`'s `ptr u8 from room`; D199"
               & " converts neither bytes nor a pointer to `cstring`, so a"
               & " `cstring` parameter could not be filled there at all. P"
               & "ortable paths are host strings through `platform/posix`,"
               & " and the raw wrappers serve that module and programs tha"
               & "t hold bytes. A program with a literal binds it, `name: "
               & "[]u8 = ""/etc/hostname""`, and passes `addr name[0]`: the "
               & "literal ends in NUL [0260], and the pointer keeps the li"
               & "teral's static origin. L0301 gives that route when a lit"
               & "eral meets a `ptr u8` context, and names `cstring` among"
               & " a literal's contexts.",
            when 444 =>
               "Chosen: `core/fibre` has three layers. The switch, `prep"
               & "are` and `switch` over a caller's record and stack, is f"
               & "or whoever writes a provider. Two concepts say what a pr"
               & "ovider is: `scheduler`, whose `start` may run a task to "
               & "its end before returning and whose `wait` returns once o"
               & "ne of its fibres has finished, or at once when none is r"
               & "unning; and `turns`, a `scheduler` that adds `yield`, wh"
               & "ose contract is that a fibre that yields lets every othe"
               & "r unfinished fibre of the provider run before it resumes"
               & ". A provider that runs everything to its end has no `yie"
               & "ld`, so a program that needs turns says so in the concep"
               & "t it asks for and is refused where it asks. The blocking"
               & " host and `fibre.whole` provide `scheduler`; a device's "
               & "round of turns, the event-driven Io and an RTOS's schedu"
               & "ler provide `turns`. The library carries the switch, `wh"
               & "ole` and one round of fixed turns over caller records, w"
               & "ith the wait when nobody can run supplied by the provide"
               & "r built on it; priorities, timers and preemption stay ou"
               & "t of it."
               & LF
               & LF
               & "An application uses the third layer only. `group_over` t"
               & "akes a `scheduler` and `turns_over` a `turns`, with a ba"
               & "cking the caller lends and a count, and cuts the backing"
               & " into equal stacks; the group comes `from` the provider "
               & "and the backing. `admit` waits, through the provider, fo"
               & "r a free stack, copies the task's state onto it as a cal"
               & "l passes an argument, and starts a fibre that calls an o"
               & "rdinary routine with that copy; one group holds tasks of"
               & " different state types. A task's error set is `failure.r"
               & "eason`: the group keeps the first failure and `join` fai"
               & "ls with it, after every admitted task has ended, since n"
               & "othing cancels a fibre. A task with atoms of its own map"
               & "s them before returning, as `core/failure` asks of a set"
               & " that holds both. A group must be joined before its back"
               & "ing goes, and the program's `defer` does it, as it relea"
               & "ses a region.",
            when 448 =>
               "Chosen: on one core, an operation in flight is a request"
               & " whose answering has started and not finished. A device "
               & "answers in arrival order, one at a time, and answers `bu"
               & "sy` when the requests waiting for it fill its queue; rec"
               & "eiving goes on in a fibre of its own. Fibres on a device"
               & " are for structure, taking input while answering, and no"
               & "t for overlapping answers. A trace of the derived firmwa"
               & "re shows answers in request order, none starting before "
               & "the previous one has finished.",
            when 449 =>
               "Chosen: nothing cancels a fibre. A program stops one by "
               & "failing the I/O it waits on: an Io that runs fibres wake"
               & "s every fibre waiting on a descriptor when it is shut or"
               & " closed through the provider, and the woken call fails `"
               & "io_failed`; a signal reaches the provider as an event re"
               & "ad by an entry that waits like a receive, never as a han"
               & "dler running Landin code on a fibre's stack. A fibre tha"
               & "t never ends holds its group's `join` for ever, and one "
               & "never resumed never runs its `defer`s; both are stated, "
               & "not prevented. An interrupt handler never switches: it r"
               & "ecords what happened for the provider to see before it w"
               & "aits. The atomic wrapper names the single-writer update,"
               & " a load and a store, as an operation of its own on every"
               & " target, and refuses a shared read-modify-write where th"
               & "e target has none, naming the critical section. The fake"
               & " network, given a scheduler that takes turns, yields whe"
               & "re a call would wait and answers `timed_out` only after "
               & "a whole round in which nothing it waits for arrived; wit"
               & "hout one it behaves as now, and the library reference's "
               & "reason is reworded.",
            when 463 =>
               "Chosen: `core/fibre` holds the concepts `task`, `schedul"
               & "er` and `turns`, the record `space`, `whole` and the gro"
               & "up, and calls no builtin. The switch, `prepare` and `swi"
               & "tch`, and the round of fixed turns built on it, `round`,"
               & " are the submodule `core/fibre/stacks`, as `core/io/fake"
               & "` is `core/io`'s. A program that never switches a stack,"
               & " a group over `whole` or over the blocking host, is then"
               & " admitted on every target, firmware and synthetic-32 inc"
               & "luded; one that imports `core/fibre/stacks` is admitted "
               & "where its backend emits the builtins. `hosted/system` pr"
               & "ovides `fibre.scheduler` in a file of its own and import"
               & "s `core/fibre` and not its switch, so no hosted target i"
               & "s refused for it. There is no import cycle: `core/fibre`"
               & " imports `core/failure` for its error set and `core/mem`"
               & ", and neither imports anything hosted. The price is the "
               & "closure: every hosted program now reaches `core/fibre`, "
               & "`core/failure` and the `core/map` and `core/tree` that `"
               & "core/failure` names atoms from, which made a hosted prog"
               & "ram's debug compile about a tenth slower when it was mea"
               & "sured and its executable no larger.",
            when 464 =>
               "Chosen: four spellings and one representation, each beca"
               & "use the sketch's would not compile or would not hold. `t"
               & "ask`'s entry is `run: (self: ptr mut task_type) -> none`"
               & ": an `inout self` has no erased table (D146), and a prov"
               & "ider is handed `any task`. The switch's, the providers' "
               & "and the group's failure is `mem.out_of_memory`, where th"
               & "e sketch had `stack_too_small | stack_misaligned`: `fail"
               & "ure.reason` must hold whatever `admit` fails with, which"
               & " would make `core/failure` import `core/fibre`; a stack "
               & "is aligned by `stack_prepare` and never misaligned; and "
               & "caller-lent backing too small for its use is out of memo"
               & "ry, as `core/arena`'s and `core/pool`'s is. `prepare` ta"
               & "kes a fourth record, `after`, the one a fibre resumes wh"
               & "en its task has ended: the sketch's ""switches back to wh"
               & "oever started it"" is not the round's next turn, and a pr"
               & "ovider is the one that knows. A round's wait when nobody"
               & " can run is the concept `stacks.idler`, given to `round_"
               & "over`, with `stacks.spin` returning at once; it is calle"
               & "d after a whole round in which every unfinished entry yi"
               & "elded and nothing started or ended. And a group made ove"
               & "r `turns` keeps its provider as `any turns` beside an un"
               & "used `any scheduler`, because the one does not convert t"
               & "o the other.",
            when 465 =>
               "Chosen: `prepare` sets the limit 1 KiB above the stack's"
               & " lowest byte, and refuses a stack smaller than 2 KiB. Th"
               & "e check is made at a switch, inside the provider, after "
               & "the provider's own calls on the way to it, and those too"
               & "k several hundred bytes below the task's frame at the hi"
               & "gher optimization profiles; with the limit at the lowest"
               & " byte, a task's overflow reached its own record, below t"
               & "he stack, before any switch read the limit from it, and "
               & "the program ran on into a fault. With the room, a task w"
               & "hose calls go a little past the limit between two switch"
               & "es traps `stack_exhausted` at the next before it has wri"
               & "tten below its stack. One that goes further has written "
               & "there already: the check is late, as D447 said, and the "
               & "depth report it names is what bounds a stack.",
            when 470 =>
               "Chosen: flash is the highest end of the image's flash lo"
               & "ad, and static RAM the highest end of its RAM load, alig"
               & "nment and zero fill included; a fibre's backing that the"
               & " program declares as module storage is static RAM, ident"
               & "ified by its symbol's extent, and is counted there once."
               & " The reserved RAM is static RAM and the main-stack reser"
               & "vation. A fibre's backing is the stack a group cuts for "
               & "it, its record at its base included; the peak simultaneo"
               & "us backing is the sum of the backings live at once, whic"
               & "h for a group is every stack it cut from admission to jo"
               & "in. A fibre's peak is the deepest byte written below its"
               & " stack's top in a run of the consumer, read from paint l"
               & "aid before the group cuts the backing, and it fits when "
               & "that peak and D461's thirty-six bytes lie within the sta"
               & "ck above the record. The consumer fits the profile when "
               & "its flash is at most 32 KiB, its reserved RAM at most 16"
               & " KiB, its main stack's painted peak within the reservati"
               & "on and every fibre fits. Paint is an observation of this"
               & " consumer's run, not a bound on any stack (D447), and a "
               & "stack's limit, its base and D472's margin, is a trap, no"
               & "t a measure of depth.",
            when 473 =>
               "Chosen: `fibre.space` keeps where its stack pointer was "
               & "saved and its status, and no limit; `stacks.switch` name"
               & "s neither record's limit; and `stacks.prepare` keeps no "
               & "room of its own. It fails `mem.out_of_memory` for a stac"
               & "k smaller than 128 words beside its `starting`, which ho"
               & "lds the first frame and the margin of every target of th"
               & "at word size, 976 bytes at most of 1,024 on the 64-bit t"
               & "argets and 432 of 512 on Cortex-M0, so a stack too small"
               & " is out of memory, as D464 has it, rather than the built"
               & "in's trap. How deep a task goes is the stack's business:"
               & " a deeper one traps at the routine that overflows. `runt"
               & "ime/fibre-same-source-any-provider` keeps the 8 KiB stac"
               & "ks its task needs on RV64, where it takes 4.1 to 4.4 KiB"
               & " at every profile: 4 KiB stacks would now trap `stack_ex"
               & "hausted` there instead of writing below the stack. For t"
               & "he same reason the 4 KiB stacks of `runtime/fibre-turns-"
               & "interleave` and `runtime/fibre-join-first-failure` becam"
               & "e 8 and 5 KiB: their tasks went deeper than 4 KiB less t"
               & "he margin on RV64, into D465's room, which the late chec"
               & "k let them use. On the retained Cortex-M0 profile the me"
               & "asured consumer (D470) no longer needs D465's 2 KiB: its"
               & " two fibres fit on backings of 1,472 bytes where they ha"
               & "d 2,176, painted to at most 904 at every profile, and it"
               & "s reserved RAM fell from 8,576 to 7,168 bytes; the check"
               & "s cost it 744 bytes of flash at `none` and 864 at `size`"
               & ".",
            when 476 =>
               "Chosen: three modules. `hosted/system` keeps the service"
               & "s that do not wait and are the same whoever waits: the a"
               & "rguments, the environment, opening and closing files, di"
               & "rectories, running programs, entropy and the wall clock,"
               & " and the last-error and last-signal cells. It is no long"
               & "er a world, because reading and writing can wait. `hoste"
               & "d/blocking` is the provider whose waiting operations blo"
               & "ck the thread: reading and writing, the network, the mon"
               & "otonic clock's `sleep`, and `fibre.scheduler`, running e"
               & "ach task to its end. `hosted/events` is the provider who"
               & "se waiting operations switch fibres over the system's ev"
               & "ent mechanism. Each of the two is built over a `hosted/s"
               & "ystem` handle and supplies `io.world` and the concepts t"
               & "he system supplies, by handing it what does not wait. A "
               & "program mints its root from the one it chooses, `blockin"
               & "g.new()` or `events.new(...)`; a program that never wait"
               & "s on anything may still use `system.new()` alone. Every "
               & "hosted source and document moves from `system.new()` to "
               & "`blocking.new()`. D479 amends this list: starting a prog"
               & "ram stays with the system, and reading its pipes and wai"
               & "ting for it are the waiting providers'.",
            when 477 =>
               "Chosen: `core/io`'s `signals` concept is provided only b"
               & "y providers of `fibre.turns`. A program that waits for a"
               & " signal asks for both, so over `hosted/blocking` it cann"
               & "ot be written and the process keeps the system's default"
               & " disposition: SIGTERM ends it. Prototype 5's derived ser"
               & "ver takes its signal waiter only when it was given a pro"
               & "vider of turns, and the choice is made where the provide"
               & "rs are minted.",
            when 478 =>
               "Chosen: `hosted/system` supplies `files`, `process`, `en"
               & "vironment`, `directories`, `programs`, `file_system`, `t"
               & "erminals`, `entropy` and `time.wall_clock`. `process` is"
               & " the standard streams' descriptors and the arguments, wh"
               & "ich do not wait; reading a stream does. `file_system`'s "
               & "`read_at` and `write_at` stay with it, because a regular"
               & " file is always ready and no event mechanism waits on on"
               & "e. `programs` stays with it as D476 says, its pipes read"
               & " and written and its children waited for by blocking the"
               & " thread whatever provider is built over it. Entropy stay"
               & "s with it: `getrandom` waits only once, at boot, for a p"
               & "ool no event announces. D479 amends the placement of `pr"
               & "ograms`: the waiting providers supply it, and the system"
               & " keeps only `start`, which they build on. `hosted/blocki"
               & "ng` supplies `reader`, `writer` and so `world`, `net.net"
               & "work`, the monotonic `time.clock`, since `now` cannot be"
               & " supplied without `sleep`, and `fibre.scheduler`, and su"
               & "pplies every concept of the system's by calling the syst"
               & "em's own entry on its handle. Its handle is a struct hol"
               & "ding the system's; there is one last-error cell, the sys"
               & "tem handle's, which `hosted/system` lets a provider buil"
               & "t over it clear and fill with `clear_errno` and `record_"
               & "errno`, and `is_socket` tells such a provider which of t"
               & "he system's files it writes by sending. The file encodin"
               & "g, `descriptor_of`, `file_of` and `socket_of`, stays the"
               & " system's alone, so a program that converts a descriptor"
               & " imports both modules.",
            when 479 =>
               "Chosen: `io.programs` keeps its one shape, and the provi"
               & "ders that wait supply it, as they supply reading and wri"
               & "ting: `hosted/blocking` and `hosted/events`, each in its"
               & " `programs.ldn`. `write_child`, `read_child` and `wait` "
               & "are the entries that wait; `spawn` and `close_input` do "
               & "not. Starting a child stays in `hosted/system`, as the p"
               & "ublic routine `system.start(handle, path, arguments, env"
               & "ironment, streams)`, which makes the pipes and `/dev/nul"
               & "l`, calls `posix.spawn`, maps its errno onto the concept"
               & "'s atoms in the handle's last-error cell, and answers an"
               & " `io.child` whose pipes are files of the system's, which"
               & " the provider reads, writes and closes as its own. `syst"
               & "em.process_of` gives the child's `posix.process_id` for "
               & "the provider to wait for, and `system.ended` turns the s"
               & "tatus it waited for into `io.ending`, keeping the signal"
               & " in the handle's last-signal cell. `hosted/system` is no"
               & " provider of `io.programs`. The blocking provider polls "
               & "both output pipes and reads with its `read`, as before; "
               & "the event provider sets the parent's ends non-blocking a"
               & "nd waits on them as on any file, and waits for the end o"
               & "f a child through `pidfd_open` on Linux (D487), and kque"
               & "ue's `EVFILT_PROC` with `NOTE_EXIT`, which `platform/kqu"
               & "eue` names as `note_exit`, on Darwin and FreeBSD, before"
               & " reaping it with a `wait` that does not block. This amen"
               & "ds D476's list of the system's services and D478's place"
               & "ment of `programs`."
               & LF
               & LF
               & "`posix.spawn` starts every child with an empty signal ma"
               & "sk, on Linux by `rt_sigprocmask` in the child between th"
               & "e copy and the exec, and on Darwin and FreeBSD by `posix"
               & "_spawnattr_setsigmask` with `POSIX_SPAWN_SETSIGMASK`. Be"
               & "side SIGPIPE, which D322 already gives back, it gives th"
               & "e child the default disposition of each signal named to "
               & "`posix.default_in_children(signal)`, which a provider ca"
               & "lls for every signal it takes from its disposition; `POS"
               & "IX_SPAWN_SETSIGDEF` carries them on Darwin and FreeBSD, "
               & "and `rt_sigaction` in the Linux child. A signal nobody n"
               & "amed keeps whatever disposition the parent gives it, so "
               & "a shell's background job, started with SIGINT ignored, a"
               & "nd a program under `nohup` pass their ignores on as POSI"
               & "X programs do. `default_in_children` refuses with `einva"
               & "l` a number that is no signal, one past 64 or Darwin's 3"
               & "1, and SIGKILL and SIGSTOP, which a child could not be g"
               & "iven.",
            when 480 =>
               "Chosen: the loop's sleep is the wait's own time limit: `"
               & "epoll_pwait`'s milliseconds, a part of one counting as a"
               & " whole one, and `kevent`'s `timespec`. A fibre's deadlin"
               & "e is kept by the provider and checked against the monoto"
               & "nic clock when the wait returns, so a limit rounded up w"
               & "akes the loop late by less than a millisecond and never "
               & "early. Nothing outside the loop's own thread can make it"
               & " ready while there is one thread and no handler runs Lan"
               & "din code (D449), so there is no waking descriptor. `plat"
               & "form/linux` therefore wraps `epoll_create1`, `epoll_ctl`"
               & ", `epoll_pwait`, `signalfd4` and `rt_sigprocmask` and ne"
               & "ither `eventfd2` nor the timerfd calls, and `platform/kq"
               & "ueue` names the timer filter, which a program may use, a"
               & "nd not the user filter. Their numbers stay in `platform/"
               & "linux/numbers` for a program that wants them.",
            when 481 =>
               "Chosen: `platform/kqueue`, one file, `kqueue.ldn`, decla"
               & "ring `kqueue`, `kevent`, each system's `struct kevent` a"
               & "s `event_record`, the filters and flags the two share an"
               & "d each system's timer units under `compiler.os`, and not"
               & "hing on Linux. Its scope is the hosted POSIX systems, Li"
               & "nux included, as `platform/linux`'s is, so a provider wr"
               & "itten once imports both and selects its own routines by "
               & "`compiler.os`; firmware refuses it by name. It imports `"
               & "platform/libc` for `timespec` and leaves the errno to `l"
               & "ibc.errno_cell`. The calls a signal waiter needs beside "
               & "it, `sigprocmask`, `kill` and `getpid`, are every system"
               & "'s C library's and are declared in `platform/libc`.",
            when 482 =>
               "Chosen: the concept is `signals` in `core/io/signal`, a "
               & "module beneath `core/io` as `core/io/fake` is, which imp"
               & "orts `core/fibre` and `core/io`: `signals: type = concep"
               & "t (provider: type) is fibre.turns`. Its entries are `wat"
               & "ch`, which takes one signal from the system's default di"
               & "sposition and delivers it as an event from then on; `nex"
               & "t_signal`, which waits, taking turns, for the next arriv"
               & "al; and `stop_watching`, which gives every watched signa"
               & "l back to its default disposition and wakes every waiter"
               & ", whose call fails `io_failed`, as D449 stops a fibre by"
               & " failing what it waits on. Only `next_signal` switches. "
               & "A signal is named by the atom set `kind`: `interrupt`, `"
               & "terminate`, `hangup`, `child`, `user1` and `user2`, the "
               & "six a server cares about, and an arrival is an `event` o"
               & "f its `kind` and the system's own number. One signal at "
               & "a time is watched, so both mechanisms implement it direc"
               & "tly: signalfd adds it to the blocked mask and the descri"
               & "ptor's set, kqueue ignores it and adds an `EVFILT_SIGNAL"
               & "` filter. Two arrivals before a read may be one event, a"
               & "s both systems keep them. The fake, `fake.signals`, is g"
               & "iven the turns it waits on and passes `fibre.turns`' ent"
               & "ries to them, so it is a provider of both; `raise` deliv"
               & "ers a signal into it, one nobody watches is counted and "
               & "dropped, and it numbers signals as Linux does on x86-64 "
               & "and arm64."
               & LF
               & LF
               & "Writing this found that the checker counted only a paren"
               & "t concept written as a bare name: a parent named through"
               & " its module, `fibre.turns` here, `io.reader` beneath `ne"
               & "t.network`, was skipped, so a conformance to the child w"
               & "as accepted without one to the parent. The concept body'"
               & "s parents now include a qualified reference, as its acce"
               & "ssor's postcondition already said.",
            when 483 =>
               "Chosen: `network_over_turns(state, sockets, runs)` makes"
               & " the network over a `fibre.turns` it borrows for as long"
               & " as it is used, beside `network_over`, which keeps a sch"
               & "eduler that is never called and waits for nothing. A cal"
               & "l that would wait, `accept`, `send`, `receive`, `receive"
               & "_from` and the reader and writer entries over them, yiel"
               & "ds and looks again. The network counts in `moves` each c"
               & "hange something could wait for: a connection made or tak"
               & "en, bytes or a datagram delivered or taken, a shutdown a"
               & "nd a close. A call that yielded and finds `moves` unchan"
               & "ged has seen a whole round of every other fibre in which"
               & " nothing moved, and so nothing it waits for arrived, and"
               & " fails `timed_out`; one that finds it changed looks agai"
               & "n. A call whose socket was closed, or shut for receiving"
               & ", while it waited fails `io_failed` when it wakes, as D4"
               & "49 asks of an Io that runs fibres. `turns` counts the tu"
               & "rns its calls took.",
            when 485 =>
               "Chosen: `events.new(state, entries)` fills an `events.sp"
               & "ace` the caller declares `zeroed`, the round's state and"
               & " the event loop's, and returns a handle `from state, ent"
               & "ries`, where `entries` is the round's table, one more th"
               & "an the fibres that may be unfinished at once. It fails `"
               & "mem.out_of_memory` for a table of fewer than two and `io"
               & "_failed` when the system makes no queue. The handle runs"
               & " its fibres on core/fibre/stacks' `round`, whose idler i"
               & "s the loop, and passes the round's entries on through th"
               & "eir evidence, so it is a `fibre.turns`. An operation tha"
               & "t waits fills a record on its own fibre's stack, links i"
               & "t into the loop's list and takes turns until the loop an"
               & "swers it: the fibre does not return from the call before"
               & " then, so the list never holds a record whose frame has "
               & "gone, and the provider needs no table of waits for the c"
               & "aller to size. The hosted/system handle beneath is the p"
               & "rocess's, `system.new()`, as `blocking.new()`'s is, so `"
               & "last_errno` reads the process's cell. The queue is close"
               & "d on exec and stays open until the process ends; there i"
               & "s no call that closes it.",
            when 486 =>
               "Chosen: a waiting record names a descriptor and a direct"
               & "ion, a child (kqueue's), a signal or a deadline on the m"
               & "onotonic clock, and the loop answers it `ready`, `expire"
               & "d` or `failed`; the operation then makes its call again."
               & " Submitting arms the descriptor once, `EPOLLONESHOT` for"
               & " the union of the directions every record on it waits fo"
               & "r and kqueue's `EV_ONESHOT` per filter, and after a repo"
               & "rt the loop arms it again for the records still waiting."
               & " The round calls the loop when every fibre has taken a t"
               & "urn since anything last started or ended. The loop then "
               & "waits without a limit, until the earliest deadline, or n"
               & "ot at all when a fibre took a turn of its own through `y"
               & "ield`, which is runnable work; with no record waiting an"
               & "d no such turn it returns at once. Closing a file, a soc"
               & "ket or a child's pipe through the provider answers every"
               & " record on its descriptor `failed` and removes it from e"
               & "poll before the descriptor closes; shutting a socket's s"
               & "ide answers that side's records. The provider's sockets "
               & "and a child's pipes are non-blocking; a file it did not "
               & "make, a standard stream or a file opened by path, is pol"
               & "led with no limit first and read or written once ready, "
               & "so a regular file, always ready, is read at once, and th"
               & "e program's terminal is never made non-blocking behind i"
               & "ts shell. A socket's limits are kept as the system's own"
               & " time limits, which a non-blocking socket never waits on"
               & ", and each wait reads them back, `platform/posix`'s `sen"
               & "d_timeout` beside `receive_timeout`; a limit the system "
               & "does not give back, as QEMU's user emulation does not, i"
               & "s none. A connect has no limit.",
            when 487 =>
               "Chosen: on Linux the provider opens a pidfd for the chil"
               & "d, waits for it to be readable as for any descriptor, cl"
               & "oses it and reaps the child with `posix.wait`; a kernel "
               & "without `pidfd_open`, before 5.3, has the reap wait the "
               & "thread instead. On Darwin and FreeBSD it adds a one-shot"
               & " `EVFILT_PROC` filter for `note_exit`, and a child the q"
               & "ueue refuses with ESRCH has ended already and is reaped "
               & "at once. `spawn` starts the child through the system han"
               & "dle and sets the parent's pipe ends non-blocking; `read_"
               & "child` reads the output when it has anything, its end in"
               & "cluded, then the errors, and when neither is ready waits"
               & " for both and goes on with whichever the loop answers fi"
               & "rst.",
            when 488 =>
               "Chosen: on Linux one signalfd reads every watched signal"
               & ", its mask growing with each `watch`, and the loop watch"
               & "es it from the first. On Darwin and FreeBSD each watched"
               & " signal is ignored and reported by an `EVFILT_SIGNAL` fi"
               & "lter, except SIGCHLD, whose default already ignores it: "
               & "an ignored SIGCHLD reaps every child before `wait` could"
               & ". Each signal is named to `posix.default_in_children` be"
               & "fore it is taken, so no child keeps the block or the ign"
               & "ore. The loop keeps each arrival in order of arrival, tw"
               & "o of one signal before a read being one, until a fibre r"
               & "eads it with `next_signal`, which waits as a receive doe"
               & "s. `stop_watching` first reads what arrived, so that unb"
               & "locking a signal that came while it was watched does not"
               & " deliver it with its default, then closes the signalfd, "
               & "unblocks or restores every watched signal, forgets the a"
               & "rrivals and fails every waiter `io_failed`; a later `nex"
               & "t_signal` fails at once until `watch` is called again.",
            when 489 =>
               "Chosen: `examples/derived_server` has the sketch's four "
               & "modules. Its `app` reads `--io=blocking` or `--io=events"
               & "` and `--port=N` through a `hosted/system` handle, and i"
               & "ts two minting routines are the only code that knows whi"
               & "ch provider it got. Over the blocking provider it calls "
               & "`server.serve`, which announces the address and serves w"
               & "ith no signal waiter, so SIGTERM ends the process by its"
               & " default disposition. Over a provider of turns and signa"
               & "ls it calls `server.serve_until_terminated`, which watch"
               & "es SIGTERM, announces, and runs a fibre that waits for t"
               & "he signal, then shuts both directions of every connectio"
               & "n being served and closes the listener; the accept and e"
               & "very receive fail `io_failed` (D449), and the server end"
               & "s cleanly, with the count of requests it answered, only "
               & "when the waiter stopped it. Such a provider is lent thre"
               & "e ways, as `fibre.turns`, `signal.signals` and `fibre.sc"
               & "heduler`, since the three do not convert (D464). An `any"
               & " C` is a provider of C and of the concepts C refines (D4"
               & "92), so the erased network goes to `net`'s routines, `io"
               & ".lines_over` and `io.buffered_over`, and the erased cloc"
               & "k to `protocol.answer`, generic over its clock, as the s"
               & "ketch wrote them, with no adapter. The protocol separate"
               & "s words by one space, takes a tag of at least one byte a"
               & "nd no space, and refuses a wait over a minute; every oth"
               & "er line, one too long for the session's buffer among the"
               & "m, is answered `malformed`.",
            when 490 =>
               "Chosen: the fixture's program is both parts. Run without"
               & " arguments it is the harness: it starts itself again thr"
               & "ough `io.programs`, by `posix.program_name()`, with `ser"
               & "ve`, the provider's `--io=` and `--port=0`, and the chil"
               & "d calls the same `app.entry` as the example's `main`. Th"
               & "e harness reads the child's first output line for the ad"
               & "dress, sends `WAIT 1000 a` on one connection and `NOW b`"
               & " on another, and reads the second with a receive limit o"
               & "f 500 milliseconds: an answer within it came before `a`,"
               & " which the server sends no sooner than 1000 milliseconds"
               & " after it was asked, and none means `a` came first. It n"
               & "eeds no turns, so it runs over the blocking provider on "
               & "every hosted target. It sends SIGTERM, `kill` on Darwin "
               & "and FreeBSD and the system call on Linux, reads the rest"
               & " of the child's output and waits for it: over the blocki"
               & "ng provider the child must have been ended by the signal"
               & " and written nothing more. The same exchange then runs w"
               & "ith `--io=events`, over `hosted/events`, and requires `b"
               & "` first, `stopped after 2 requests` as the child's last "
               & "line and status 0: the server's signal waiter, not the s"
               & "ignal's default, ended it. The server's source is the sa"
               & "me in both children; only `app`'s minting routine differ"
               & "s. The QEMU cross lanes, which cannot start the program'"
               & "s own child without a binfmt_misc handler, list the fixt"
               & "ure in `compiler/tests/cross-lanes.json`.",
            when 493 =>
               "Chosen: `clock_beside(state, start, wall, network)` make"
               & "s `core/io/fake`'s manual clock beside a network, and ov"
               & "er a network that takes turns its `sleep` takes the netw"
               & "ork's turns. While it sleeps the network counts it in `s"
               & "leepers`, and a call that waited a round finding `moves`"
               & " unchanged fails `timed_out` only while `sleepers` is ze"
               & "ro. The clock moves only after a whole round in which no"
               & "thing in the network moved, when every other fibre waite"
               & "d: the sleeper that saw the round advances it by a milli"
               & "second, or by what is left of its sleep when that is les"
               & "s, and counts the advance in `moves`, so a second sleepe"
               & "r in the same round does not advance it again and sleepe"
               & "rs wake in the order of their deadlines, to the millisec"
               & "ond. Beside a network that takes no turns, and from `clo"
               & "ck_over`, the clock is as before: `sleep` advances it at"
               & " once. The only new surface is the constructor and the `"
               & "sleepers` count.",
            when 494 =>
               "Chosen: `hosted/thread` starts threads as `core/fibre`'s"
               & " application layer starts fibres. A group is made over a"
               & " `hosted/system` handle, a backing the caller lends and "
               & "a count; `admit` copies a task's state onto a free stack"
               & " and starts a thread that calls an ordinary routine with"
               & " that copy, waiting for a stack to come free when none i"
               & "s; the group keeps the first failure in a ledger the thr"
               & "eads share through the atomic wrapper, and `join` fails "
               & "with it once every admitted thread has ended. D445's `es"
               & "caping into` and the `defer` that joins are as for fibre"
               & "s. A successful `admit` synchronizes with the new thread"
               & "'s first action and a thread's end with the return of th"
               & "e `join` that waits for it, as D227 has it; a failed sta"
               & "rt establishes neither edge and starts nothing. A static"
               & " Linux program starts a thread with `clone` and waits fo"
               & "r its end on the word the kernel clears; under `--link=l"
               & "ibc`, on Darwin and on FreeBSD the C library starts it w"
               & "ith `pthread_create` and waits with `pthread_join`. A th"
               & "read begins with every signal blocked, so the signals a "
               & "provider reads through a signalfd or kqueue reach that p"
               & "rovider and no worker's default disposition. `join` bloc"
               & "ks the calling thread whatever provider it runs under, s"
               & "o a fibre that joins holds its round. A worker may run a"
               & " round of fibres of its own; a fibre never moves between"
               & " threads.",
            when 495 =>
               "Chosen: as a fibre group does, a thread group cuts its c"
               & "aller's backing into equal stacks and prepares each with"
               & " `compiler.stack_prepare`, so a program that starts a th"
               & "read checks every routine against the running thread's o"
               & "wn limit (D497) and a worker past its stack traps `stack"
               & "_exhausted`. Where the C library starts the thread, its "
               & "own start frames and, under glibc, the thread's block ar"
               & "e placed in the same backing. A stack smaller than the s"
               & "ystem's minimum is refused when the group is made; the i"
               & "tem that implements the group records the figures. Start"
               & "ing a thread allocates nothing and maps no guard page.",
            when 500 =>
               "Chosen: `core/atomic` gives a cell over one `u8`, `u16`,"
               & " `u32` or `u64`. A load acquires and a store releases; e"
               & "xchange, add and compare-exchange are acq_rel, a failed "
               & "comparison acquiring; a relaxed family loads, stores and"
               & " adds for counters and caches; seq_cst stays with the bu"
               & "iltins. The single-writer update, a relaxed load and a r"
               & "elease store, is an operation of its own, correct while "
               & "one context writes the cell, on every target. On Cortex-"
               & "M0 exchange, add and compare-exchange are refused at the"
               & " caller's use, the refusal naming the single-writer upda"
               & "te and `platform/cortex_m`'s critical section, as are th"
               & "e eight-byte cell's operations there.",
            when 501 =>
               "Chosen: `hosted/thread` gives a lock over one word of th"
               & "e atomic wrapper, which an uncontended lock takes and gi"
               & "ves with one read-modify-write each, and which waits and"
               & " wakes through the system's own wait on an address: the "
               & "futex on Linux, `_umtx_op` on FreeBSD and `os_sync_wait_"
               & "on_address` on Darwin, which `platform/posix` names on e"
               & "ach. Waiting blocks the thread, so a fibre that holds a "
               & "lock across a switch can hold another fibre of its round"
               & ". On Cortex-M0 the critical section is the lock.",
            when 502 =>
               "Chosen: `hosted/heap`'s size classes are behind one lock"
               & " (D501). A program that has started no thread skips it: "
               & "the thread facility sets a relaxed flag before its first"
               & " start, and the creation edge orders everything the prog"
               & "ram did before. A mapping of its own needs no lock. The "
               & "vDSO cache is a relaxed atomic word, whose value every t"
               & "hread computes alike, and which D499 makes a plain move."
               & " Caches per thread are the optimization phase's.",
            when 503 =>
               "Chosen: `hosted/system`'s last-error and last-signal cel"
               & "ls are `link(thread)` storage (D496), and a handle from "
               & "`system.new()` records into the cell of the thread makin"
               & "g the call, not the one that made the handle, so handles"
               & " shared across threads keep D207's thread-local meaning;"
               & " `system.over` still records into a cell of its caller's"
               & " own. The argument and environment roots are written bef"
               & "ore `main` and only read after, which the creation edge "
               & "orders. `child_defaults` is the atomic wrapper's. The wo"
               & "rking directory and the environment are still never chan"
               & "ged. D232's panic latch stays the process's. D480 is unc"
               & "hanged: a thread that wakes a loop brings its descriptor"
               & ". Darwin's `spawn` already closes every descriptor it do"
               & "es not give the child, so a pipe made beside it in anoth"
               & "er thread leaks nothing into a program Landin starts; wh"
               & "at remains is a C library's own `exec`.",
            when 509 =>
               "Chosen: `hosted/system`'s handle holds, for each of its "
               & "two cells, D189's one-atom pointer union of `calling_thr"
               & "ead` and the caller's cell. `new` stores the atom, and e"
               & "very record and read through the handle matches it, reac"
               & "hing the `link(thread)` cells `thread_errno` and `thread"
               & "_signal` of whichever thread runs; `over` stores the cal"
               & "ler's own cells, as before. The handle stays two words, "
               & "and copies share what they were made with.",
            when 510 =>
               "Chosen: `core/atomic` gives each of `u8`, `u16`, `u32` a"
               & "nd `u64` a conformance to its concept `scalar` and to `e"
               & "xchangeable`, which refines it, only where the target ca"
               & "rries those accesses: under `fixed if compiler.arch <> c"
               & "ortex_m0` for `u64` and for every `exchangeable`. A cell"
               & "'s type is constrained by `scalar`, and its exchange, ad"
               & "d, relaxed add and compare-exchange by `exchangeable`, s"
               & "o on Cortex-M0 the missing conformance is found where th"
               & "e program writes the cell's type or calls the operation,"
               & " not in the library's bodies, which the target never che"
               & "cks. The checker says such a missing conformance of one "
               & "of `core/atomic`'s concepts for one of the four scalars "
               & "as the target's refusal, L0344, at that use: when the ta"
               & "rget has no atomic access of the scalar's width, that it"
               & " has no cell of it, naming a cell of four bytes or fewer"
               & " and the critical section; when it has the accesses but "
               & "no read-modify-write, that a cell has no exchange, add o"
               & "r compare-exchange there, naming `atomic.sole_add` and t"
               & "he critical section. Which refusal it is comes from the "
               & "target's own admission of the builtins (D227), not from "
               & "a list of targets. Any other type is L0318 at its use, i"
               & "ts note saying a cell holds a `u8`, `u16`, `u32` or `u64"
               & "`. The concept is recognized by the module that declares"
               & " it, as [0610]'s `core/text.position` is.",
            when 511 =>
               "Chosen: `atomic.cell(T)` is a struct of one field, opaqu"
               & "e outside the module, which module storage starts `zeroe"
               & "d` and `atomic.new(value)` makes for a local or a field."
               & " Its operations take the cell's address: `load` and `sto"
               & "re`, acquiring and releasing; `load_relaxed`, `store_rel"
               & "axed` and `add_relaxed`; `exchange`, `add` and `compare_"
               & "exchange`, which return what the cell held, an add wrapp"
               & "ing at the scalar's width. The single-writer update is `"
               & "atomic.sole_add(cell, value)`: a relaxed load, a release"
               & " store of the wrapping sum, and what the cell held, corr"
               & "ect while one context alone writes the cell, and on ever"
               & "y target. Each operation calls its concept's entry, whic"
               & "h `--specialize` makes a direct call, so a cell operatio"
               & "n costs a call more than the builtin until the inliner t"
               & "akes it. The name is provisional: `sole_add` was chosen "
               & "to say in the operation's own name that it has one write"
               & "r, which `advance` would not, and its shape, an add rath"
               & "er than an update taking a routine, because the consumer"
               & " it serves is a count and a handler should not call thro"
               & "ugh a function value.",
            when 512 =>
               "Chosen: `posix.wait_on(word, expected)` sleeps while the"
               & " `atomic.cell(u32)` at `word` holds `expected`, and `pos"
               & "ix.wait_on_within(word, expected, span)` does for at mos"
               & "t a span on the monotonic clock, failing `etimedout` aft"
               & "er it and `einval` for a span no `time_value` may be; `p"
               & "osix.wake_one(word)` and `posix.wake_all(word)` wake one"
               & " or every waiter. The word is four bytes, the one width "
               & "all three systems wait on, and private to the process. E"
               & "ither wait returns at once when the cell does not hold `"
               & "expected`, and may return with nobody having woken it, s"
               & "o a waiter reads the cell again; neither has any other f"
               & "ailure, since the systems' others are an address the cel"
               & "l's type rules out. On Linux they are `platform/linux`'s"
               & " `futex_wait` and `futex_wake` over `FUTEX_WAIT_PRIVATE`"
               & " and `FUTEX_WAKE_PRIVATE`, the operations private to the"
               & " module; on FreeBSD `_umtx_op` with `UMTX_OP_WAIT_UINT_P"
               & "RIVATE` and `UMTX_OP_WAKE_PRIVATE`, a span given as a `s"
               & "truct _umtx_time` on `CLOCK_MONOTONIC`; on Darwin `os_sy"
               & "nc_wait_on_address`, its `_with_timeout` form on `OS_CLO"
               & "CK_MACH_ABSOLUTE_TIME`, and `os_sync_wake_by_address_any"
               & "` and `_all`, which macOS 14.4 added.",
            when 513 =>
               "Chosen: `hosted/thread/lock` is a module beneath `hosted"
               & "/thread`, so that the heap can import it without importi"
               & "ng the facility, which never imports the heap. A `lock.l"
               & "ock` is one `u32` cell, free, taken, or taken with a thr"
               & "ead waiting, as Drepper's ""Futexes Are Tricky"" gives it:"
               & " `lock.take` takes a free lock with one compare-exchange"
               & ", and otherwise marks it waited for with an exchange and"
               & " waits on the cell until an exchange finds it free; `loc"
               & "k.give` frees it with one exchange and wakes one waiter "
               & "when it was waited for; `lock.take_if_free` never waits."
               & " A zeroed lock is free. It is neither reentrant nor owne"
               & "d. The flag is a relaxed `u32` cell of the module's, set"
               & " by `lock.note_start()`, which the thread facility calls"
               & " before its first start, and read by `lock.threads_start"
               & "ed()`. On Cortex-M0 there is no lock: the critical secti"
               & "on is one.",
            when 514 =>
               "Chosen: `hosted/heap` reads the flag once for each slot "
               & "it takes or gives, and takes the lock around the class's"
               & " list, mapping a chunk under it; a block larger than the"
               & " largest class takes none. Measured on Linux x86-64 with"
               & " the debug compiler, twenty million allocations and free"
               & "s of 24 bytes, each pair: at `--optimize size` 78 ns bef"
               & "ore, 197 ns with the flag clear and 460 ns with it set; "
               & "at `--optimize speed` 28 ns, 145 ns and 367 ns. Those fi"
               & "gures predate D499, under which every atomic was fenced "
               & "before and after. With D499's lowering, measured again o"
               & "n the merged item the same way, three runs each: at `siz"
               & "e` 76 ns before, 100 ns with the flag clear and 135 ns w"
               & "ith it set; at `speed` 27.5 ns, 37.7 ns and 53.6 ns. The"
               & " flag is a plain load now, and what a pair still pays wi"
               & "th it clear is the register's to find. The vDSO cache is"
               & " a relaxed `u64` cell, a plain move (D317), and `child_d"
               & "efaults` is a `u64` cell a compare-exchange adds a signa"
               & "l to and a spawn reads once with an acquiring load.",
            when 517 =>
               "Chosen: each of a group's stacks holds its record at its"
               & " base, the task's own stack above it with the task's sta"
               & "te at that part's top, and, at the stack's top, the area"
               & " the thread starts on. A static Linux program calls `clo"
               & "ne` with `CLONE_VM`, `CLONE_FS`, `CLONE_FILES`, `CLONE_S"
               & "IGHAND`, `CLONE_THREAD`, `CLONE_SYSVSEM`, `CLONE_PARENT_"
               & "SETTID` and `CLONE_CHILD_CLEARTID`, and `CLONE_SETTLS` w"
               & "ith the thread's own block, on that area; the thread's f"
               & "irst routine runs there, calls `hosted/thread`'s, and en"
               & "ds with the thread's own `exit`, never `exit_group`, so "
               & "the kernel clears the record's word and wakes a futex wa"
               & "iter only once nothing of the thread runs. `join` waits "
               & "with `FUTEX_WAIT` on that word, not the private form, be"
               & "cause the kernel's wake is not private, until an acquire"
               & " load reads zero. `platform/linux`'s `futex_wait`, which"
               & " waits private as a lock's word may, is therefore not th"
               & "e join's: a join that slept through it was never woken. "
               & "Elsewhere the C library is given the area with `pthread_"
               & "attr_setstack` and the routine with `pthread_create`, an"
               & "d `pthread_join` waits. On the area, `hosted/thread`'s r"
               & "outine first writes a `link(thread)` byte of its own, so"
               & " that Darwin's dyld makes the thread's storage there, in"
               & " a slow path no check or depth report counts, rather tha"
               & "n at a first access on the prepared stack, and then swit"
               & "ches with `compiler.stack_switch` to the prepared stack,"
               & " whose first frame runs the task and switches back; the "
               & "routine then marks the record ended and returns. Every a"
               & "synchronous signal is blocked around the start and the c"
               & "aller's mask put back after it, so the thread begins wit"
               & "h them blocked (D521).",
            when 518 =>
               "Chosen: a FreeBSD program whose reached code imports `pt"
               & "hread_create` is linked with `-lthr`, after the archives"
               & " the program asks for; one that imports none links libc "
               & "alone, as before. glibc has held its threads in libc sin"
               & "ce 2.34 and Darwin's are libSystem's, so neither needs a"
               & " library named. libthr keeps its own record of each thre"
               & "ad and its thread's storage beside the area it is given,"
               & " as Darwin's `pthread_create` does; glibc keeps both in "
               & "the area (D495).",
            when 519 =>
               "Chosen: a stack is its record, at least 4 KiB for the ta"
               & "sk's own stack, which holds `compiler.stack_prepare`'s f"
               & "irst frame and D472's margin and a few calls, and the ar"
               & "ea the thread starts on, which is the system's: 2 KiB an"
               & "d the thread's own storage on a static Linux program, fo"
               & "r the start's frames and the switch's; glibc's PTHREAD_S"
               & "TACK_MIN under `--link=libc`, 16 KiB on x86-64 and RV64 "
               & "and 128 KiB on arm64, which `pthread_attr_setstack` refu"
               & "ses below; and 16 KiB on Darwin and FreeBSD. Darwin's mi"
               & "nimum is 16 KiB too, and it takes a stack only page-alig"
               & "ned in whole 16 KiB pages, so every stack of a Darwin gr"
               & "oup is cut in whole pages and is at least 32 KiB. FreeBS"
               & "D's PTHREAD_STACK_MIN, 2 KiB on x86-64 and 4 KiB on arm6"
               & "4, is too little for libthr's own start and end, whose c"
               & "alls the run-time linker binds lazily on that stack, whi"
               & "ch took 1,664 bytes on FreeBSD arm64 (D491). `thread.lea"
               & "st_stack()` gives the figure, and `group_over` fails `me"
               & "m.out_of_memory` below it.",
            when 520 =>
               "Chosen: `admit` takes a stack no thread runs on; failing"
               & " one, it joins a thread whose task has said it ended, an"
               & "d failing that, the thread started first. A start the sy"
               & "stem refuses fails `admit` with `mem.out_of_memory`, as "
               & "POSIX's EAGAIN says the system lacked what another threa"
               & "d needs, and keeps the errno in the group's `hosted/syst"
               & "em` handle for `system.last_errno`; the stack stays free"
               & " and nothing was started. The first failure is claimed w"
               & "ith a compare-exchange on the ledger, so only one task w"
               & "rites it, and `join` reads it after every thread's end.",
            when 521 =>
               "Chosen: this amends D494's ""every signal"". A new thread "
               & "begins with every signal blocked but the six a fault rai"
               & "ses in the thread that made it: SIGILL, SIGTRAP, SIGBUS,"
               & " SIGFPE, SIGSEGV and SIGSYS, which keep the disposition "
               & "the process gives them, so a trap's terminal instruction"
               & " ends the process on every system alike. Every other sig"
               & "nal is blocked while the thread starts and in the thread"
               & ", as D494 has it; the caller's mask is put back after th"
               & "e start.",
            when 527 =>
               "Chosen: `core/io` gains `write_format`, generic over a `"
               & "writer` like `write`: a host, the file to write, a templ"
               & "ate and its values as `[]any text.formattable`, failing "
               & "`io_failed` or `text.invalid_format`. It checks the temp"
               & "late against its values before writing anything, as D355"
               & "'s `format` does, so a mismatch writes nothing. It forma"
               & "ts into a small store of its own on the stack and writes"
               & " the store to the file whenever it fills and at the end,"
               & " so a line that fits is one write and a value of any len"
               & "gth is written in pieces: it never reports `no_space`. E"
               & "very target has it. The tour prints a value with it befo"
               & "re its first loop, and keeps the buffered writer for a p"
               & "rogram that writes many pieces. An unknown `core/io` mem"
               & "ber spelt as another language's print, `print`, `println"
               & "`, `printf` or `puts`, is L0201 whose fix shows the call"
               & ". Floating-point values stay unformatted.",
            when 531 =>
               "Chosen: the release workflow takes the debug information"
               & " out of the released `refine` before packaging: `objcopy"
               & " --only-keep-debug`, a `.gnu_debuglink` and `strip --str"
               & "ip-debug` on Linux, `dsymutil` and `strip -S` on Darwin."
               & " It publishes the debug information as an asset of its o"
               & "wn beside the archive, with its checksum, and the archiv"
               & "e's layout is unchanged. The README's install route stat"
               & "es each archive's size. A released compiler's internal e"
               & "rror prints addresses, which a debugger or `addr2line` g"
               & "iven the debug asset resolves. Checkout, Nix and debug b"
               & "uilds keep their information.",
            when others => "");

end Landin.Diagnostics.Citations.Texts;
